window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["02"]={"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"c2a4809c0984d708d5fa34409f695dff62e69005323e584f682afaf4e15cec0b","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan","bytes":81907,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Azerbaijan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-27T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-23T13:44:51+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Azerbaijan-Armenia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The border with Armenia remains closed. The FCDO advises against all travel to within 5km of the border with Armenia, due to tensions between Azerbaijan and Armenia. Note that this does not include the border of Azerbaijan’s Nakhchivan exclave with Armenia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["South-western Azerbaijan (those regions affected by conflict in 2020 and 2023)"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["The districts (‘rayons’) of Kelbajar, Lachin, Qubadli, Zengilan, Jabrayil, Fuzuli, Khojavand, Shusha, Khojali, Khankendi, Aghdam and Tartar"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should follow Azerbaijani national government and local authorities’ advice in areas that have not been cleared of mines or unexploded ordnance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["UK government support"]},{"k":"p","s":["Help for British nationals is extremely limited in the areas where we advise against travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional escalation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened risk of regional tension. Escalation could lead to travel disruption, including airspace closures and other unanticipated impacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals should take sensible precautions, considering their own individual circumstances. These include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["if you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to FCDO Travel Advice email alerts"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the instructions of the local authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["For information on crossing the border from Iran into Azerbaijan, see ",["Entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Azerbaijan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Azerbaijan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Azerbaijani Embassy in the UK.","https://london.mfa.gov.az/en"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entering Azerbaijan across the land border from Iran"]},{"k":"p","s":["The border between Azerbaijan and Iran is closed. But British nationals might be able to cross at the Astara border crossing with special authorisation from the Government of Azerbaijan, which must be facilitated by the British Embassy in Baku. British nationals seeking entry into Azerbaijan should ",["contact the FCDO","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/home"]," before travelling to the border crossing at Astara, indicating whether you are contacting from Iran or from the UK on behalf of a relative. Other border crossings to Azerbaijan remain closed."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals will need to provide personal details (name, date of birth, passport information). The British Embassy will provide confirmation and a code from the Azerbaijani authorities. This can take several weeks. You should not travel to the border until you have received confirmation. You will need to show the code before crossing. You will also need to apply for a visa through the normal process. See ‘applying for a visa’."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you intend to leave Iran overland, you do so at your own risk. In Iran, holding a British passport or having perceived connections to the UK can be reason enough for the Iranian authorities to detain you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more FCDO advice ",["if you’re affected by a crisis abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Azerbaijan as a visitor, your passport must usually have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least 2 blank pages for entry stamps. See ‘visa requirements’ for more details."]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Azerbaijan as a resident, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the expiry date of your temporary or permanent residence permit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to travel on a UK Emergency Travel Document, check the visa requirements below before making your travel arrangements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Azerbaijani dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Azerbaijan does not recognise dual nationality, but does not prohibit Azerbaijani nationals from holding dual nationality. You must inform the local Azerbaijani Embassy or State Migration Service within one month of taking up another nationality. If you do not, this can impact the level of consular support FCDO will be able to provide."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British passport holder with links to Azerbaijan, through birth or otherwise, and need to check your nationality status, contact the ",["State Migration Service","https://migration.gov.az/en"]," before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["Anyone who has previously visited certain areas in south-western Azerbaijan, including the town of Khankendi, without the permission of the Azerbaijani authorities could be denied entry to Azerbaijan. You should contact the nearest embassy or consulate of Azerbaijan before you travel. See ",["Regional Risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry via land or sea borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can only enter Azerbaijan via air travel without restrictions. Entry via a land or sea border is restricted. Once in Azerbaijan you can exit via air or sea routes. If you want to leave Azerbaijan by road, you need permission from the authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entering with a vehicle"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Azerbaijan with a vehicle, you need to arrange for the vehicle to be shipped to Baku, where you have to arrange for collection at Customs. You need to provide Power of Attorney and pay fees as required."]},{"k":"h","s":["Borders with Iran and Georgia"]},{"k":"p","s":["The land borders between Iran and Azerbaijan, and Georgia and Azerbaijan are temporarily closed."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Azerbaijan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply and pay for a visa from the ",["ASAN Visa (e-visa) service","https://evisa.gov.az/en/"],". Apply at least 3 days in advance. An urgent 3-hour service is available for an additional fee."]},{"k":"p","s":["E-visas are normally single entry and allow a 30-day visit within a 90-day period of validity. You must print out the e-visa and bring it with your passport to show on arrival. Officials will check that your passport is valid for 3 months after the visa expiry date. This means your passport must be valid for at least 6 months after the date you arrive in Azerbaijan."]},{"k":"p","s":["For other types of visas, such as a business visa or a work permit, contact the ",["Azerbaijani Embassy in the UK","https://london.mfa.gov.az/en"]," at least one month before your travel date."]},{"k":"hs","s":["FIFA U-15 World Cup and Festival 2026"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to Azerbaijan for the FIFA U-15 World Cup and Festival 2026, ",["simplified visa arrangements","https://london.mfa.gov.az/en/category/facilated-visa-procedures-for-the-fifa-u-15-world-cup-festival-2026"]," are in place from 22 September to 5 November 2026. Eligible travellers can obtain a visa on arrival at Azerbaijan’s international airports. You must have either an official invitation letter from the Association of Football Federations of Azerbaijan (AFFA) or confirmation of accreditation through FIFA’s electronic registration system."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling on a UK Emergency Travel Document"]},{"k":"p","s":["Azerbaijan accepts UK Emergency Travel Documents (ETDs) for entry and must be accompanied by a visa to enter Azerbaijan. You cannot use a UK ETD to apply for an Azerbaijani e-visa, as the e-visa system does not recognise ETDs as eligible travel documents. If you are travelling on a UK ETD, you must apply for a visa directly through an Azerbaijani embassy before you travel. Contact the Azerbaijani Embassy in the country where you are applying for advice on the application process and processing times."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extending your visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can extend your 30 days by applying to the ",["State Migration Service","https://migration.gov.az/en/page/72"]," at least 3 days before the end of the permitted stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay your visa without permission, you may have to leave the country within 48 hours. Contact the ",["State Migration Service","https://migration.gov.az/en/contact/59"]," as soon as possible. They can issue a letter giving you permission to leave. You will have to pay a fine of 300 to 400 Azerbaijani manat. Make sure you get a receipt as proof of payment."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in Azerbaijan, you can also call the Migration Information Centre on 919."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying in Azerbaijan for longer than 15 days, you must ",["register with the State Migration Service","https://eservice.migration.gov.az/?lang=en"]," online or in person. If you do not register you will have to pay a fine to the ",["State Migration Service","https://migration.gov.az/en/contact/59"]," before you are able to leave the country. Hotels often provide this service for their guests, but you must do it yourself if you are staying in an apartment or private residence."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Azerbaijan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/17/azerbaijan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Azerbaijan. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty. Follow advice from your airline about items you should declare."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to use a local SIM card for more than 30 days, you must register it and pay a fee at a local post office. If you do not declare your device or register your sim card, it may not work on local networks and your device could be locked. You will need to give the IMEI number of your mobile, which you can find in settings, or by dialling *#06#."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Exporting carpets and antiques"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need an export certificate to take antiques or art like carpets, samovars, copperware or paintings out of Azerbaijan. Your vendor will give you a certificate, or they are available from the ",["Azerbaijan National Carpet Museum","https://azcarpetmuseum.az/en/contact"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Azerbaijan","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Azerbaijan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Azerbaijan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorism attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels, restaurants and pubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["energy sector facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["religious sites and places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping centres and crowded places"]},{"k":"li","s":["embassies and government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["sporting and cultural events"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport hubs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political situation in Azerbaijan is generally calm, but demonstrations and opposition rallies can occur."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid large gatherings and any demonstrations. They are illegal and there could be a swift response from the authorities. Monitor the media for information about possible demonstrations and be alert to local and regional developments, which may trigger public disturbances."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British journalist, make sure you are clearly identifiable."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Armenia-Azerbaijan tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tensions between Armenia and Azerbaijan have calmed and the risk of further conflict has decreased, including in the areas of those regions affected by conflict in 2020 and 2023. The FCDO continues to advise against all but essential travel to some areas in south-western Azerbaijan due to the risks from mines or unexploded ordnance from former conflict, and advises against all travel within 5km of the border with Armenia. See ",["Regional Risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels in Baku are generally low. Be alert to possible bag-snatching or mugging, particularly if you are carrying large amounts of cash or valuables. The risk is higher after dark in the centre of town. Avoid displaying large sums of money or expensive-looking valuables and do not walk alone at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dealing with officials"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasionally reports of government officials asking foreign nationals to make undocumented payments. If you think you have been mistreated by a traffic policeman or health professional, report your case to the relevant government department."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bank card fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fraudsters can steal your card details without you noticing. Take extra care to guard against card skimming when using credit cards or withdrawing cash from ATMs. Use ATMs inside banks where possible, check street ATMs for signs of tampering, and always keep your card in sight when paying in shops and restaurants."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Azerbaijan is a largely secular society, although most of the population is Muslim. Religion is usually considered a private matter."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some areas, such as Martyrs’ Alley, are especially sensitive. Disruptive or disrespectful conduct in or around such area may result in police action, including fines or being summoned to the police station."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police sometimes carry out checks of identity documents. Carry your passport at all times. Keep a copy of the photo page in a safe place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Baku local and foreign women usually dress in conservative western-style clothing. It is now more acceptable for men to wear shorts in Baku in the summer months. Outside of Baku it may still be frowned on, and you may receive unwelcome attention."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most restaurants, cafés, shops and other services in Azerbaijan continue to operate during Ramadan. Some businesses may adjust their opening hours or offer special Ramadan arrangements."]},{"k":"p","s":["During Ramadan, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants, as these may vary"]},{"k":"li","s":["respect local religious customs and traditions"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes, particularly when visiting religious sites - clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that some people may be fasting and may be more tired than usual, especially in the late afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and considerate towards those who are observing Ramadan"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Smoking is restricted to designated areas. You can be fined for dropping smoking-related litter. Use bins provided."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession or use of illegal drugs, including cannabis, carries severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using, or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Azerbaijan have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and drones in sensitive locations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of cultural sensitivities when photographing mosques, churches and other religious sites or sites of commemoration, such as the Alley of Martyrs in Baku. If in doubt, ask for permission."]},{"k":"p","s":["Military bases, equipment and installations in any condition are considered sensitive areas, and visitors have been detained and questioned while attempting to visit or photograph them."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not have temporary or permanent residence rights in Azerbaijan, you are not allowed to import drones. Any drones will be confiscated by the State Customs Office at the port or border and returned upon departure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unmanned drones cannot be rented to individuals without a valid taxpayer identification number (TIN). If you have a TIN, special permission from the ",["Ministry of Digital Development and Transport","https://mincom.gov.az/en"]," is required. Manned drones can be rented without requiring permission."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["While same-sex sexual activity is not illegal, LGBT+ people in Azerbaijan tend to keep a low profile. Showing affection in public is frowned upon, especially outside of Baku and among the older generation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Holding hands or embracing between men is usually a sign of friendship."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Azerbaijan, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and read the ",["RAC guide on driving in Azerbaijan","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/azerbaijan/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to use right-hand-drive cars in Azerbaijan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Inter-country road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There may be delays in transporting vehicles to Azerbaijan. It is best not to pay for non-refundable onward travel. Azerbaijan Caspian Shipping Closed Joint-Stock Company has ",["details of onward shipment from Baku to Turkmenistan and Kazakhstan","https://www.asco.az/en/pages/2/96"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Licences and permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["After one month, you will need an Azerbaijani driving licence issued through the ",["ASAN Service Offices","https://asan.gov.az/en"],". You need to carry a ",["green card","https://www.gov.uk/vehicle-insurance/driving-abroad"]," as proof you’re insured to drive in Azerbaijan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to hire a car, check with your car hire company for information on their requirements before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many vehicles are poorly maintained, and the standard of driving is erratic. Accidents are common, mainly due to poor or reckless driving and inconsistent enforcement of traffic rules. Drivers often ignore one-way signs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road closures and diversions are often unmarked. Take care when driving at night as many roads are of poor quality and badly lit. Traffic lights that are flashing amber at night mean cars can proceed with caution in either direction."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in in Azerbaijan. If you are tested and found to have any alcohol in your system, you may get a severe fine and possibly a prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the winter months snowfall often causes problems. Pack your vehicle with a blanket, shovel, torch, snacks and old carpet to help if you get stuck in snow."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Try to arrange to be picked up and dropped off as close to your hotel or apartment entrance as possible by a private or company driver, or use a known firm or taxi app."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some visitors have reported being severely overcharged by local taxis. When using taxis, agree a fare up front, or make sure the taxi meter is switched on. Check that the taxi has working seatbelts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ride-hailing apps such as Uber and Bolt are widely available in Azerbaijan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel by train, secure your valuables, do not leave the compartment unattended, and lock the door from the inside, if your compartment allows."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of earthquakes across the Caucasus region, although there have been no recent serious earthquakes in Azerbaijan. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Azerbaijan. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["South-western Azerbaijan (those regions affected by conflict in 2020 and 2023)"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) advises against all but essential travel to some areas in south-western Azerbaijan, including districts in and around the region formerly known as “Nagorno-Karabakh” due to the risks from leftover military equipment and weapons from former conflict. This includes:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the districts (‘rayons’) of Kelbajar, Lachin, Qubadli, Zengilan, Jabrayil, Fuzuli, Khojavand, Shusha, Khojali, Khankendi, Aghdam and Tartar"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to enter certain areas in south-western Azerbaijan, without the permission of the Azerbaijani authorities. Anyone who has previously visited these areas, including the town of Khankendi, without the permission of Azerbaijani authorities could be denied entry to Azerbaijan. You should contact the nearest embassy or consulate of Azerbaijan before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whilst tensions have calmed and the risk of further conflict has decreased, there remains a risk of unexploded weapons and landmines in south-western Azerbaijan. The Azerbaijani authorities are working to remove unexploded weapons and landmines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow Azerbaijani national government and local authorities’ advice in areas that have not been cleared of mines or unexploded ordnance. If you come across an unexploded weapon or landmine do not approach it or touch it. Make a note of where you saw it and notify the authorities on 102 or 112. Beware of more unexploded weapons or landmines nearby."]},{"k":"h","s":["Azerbaijan-Armenia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The border with Armenia remains closed. The FCDO also advises against all travel to within 5km of the rest of the border with Armenia. Note that this does not include the border of Azerbaijan’s Nakhchivan exclave with Armenia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Azerbaijan-Russia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The land border between Azerbaijan and Russia (Dagestan) is closed. The FCDO continues to advise against all travel to Russia. For further details, see ",["FCDO’s travel advice for Russia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/russia"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 103 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Azerbaijan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/17/azerbaijan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Go to TravelHealthPro to see ",["what health risks you’ll face in Azerbaijan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/17/azerbaijan"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in some parts of Azerbaijan, including the ski resorts of Shahdag and Tufangdag in the Gusar district, Lake Batabat in Nakhchivan, and the Talysh mountains. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare facilities in Azerbaijan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities outside Baku are very limited. Carry a comprehensive first aid kit for any trips out of Baku. Even in Baku, serious illness or injury may require evacuation to Turkey or Western Europe. Make sure you have appropriate travel health insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Azerbaijan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/azerbaijan-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Azerbaijan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 103"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 101"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 102"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=azerbaijan"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=azerbaijan"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=azerbaijan"]," in Azerbaijan"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Azerbaijan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/azerbaijan-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Azerbaijan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/azerbaijan-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/azerbaijan/british-embassy-baku"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Azerbaijan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-azerbaijan"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":25491,"change":"New information about entry requirements for the upcoming FIFA U-15 World Cup and Festival 2026 and travelling on a UK Emergency Travel Document to Azerbaijan. Updated information about visa requirements and entering Azerbaijan across the land border from Iran ('Entry requirements' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bulgaria":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"1a10ecf3da2abcb27de19ce9c4b6daab916b5a296cca9234124db96c3589a81e","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/bulgaria","bytes":78474,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Bulgaria travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-20T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:18:49+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bulgaria/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Bulgaria set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Bulgarian Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bulgaria follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must have:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the date you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carry your passport if you travel from Bulgaria to other Schengen area countries. Border guards may check it if you cross land or river borders into Greece or Romania, both in the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no routine checks when travelling by air or sea within the Schengen area, but carry your passport in case you’re asked for it. Most carriers require official photo ID."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Bulgaria, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Bulgaria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-bulgaria-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Bulgarian border control, you may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your accommodation, for example, a hotel booking confirmation or proof of address for a second home"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your travel insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay – the amount varies depending on your accommodation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, check which type of visa or work permit you need with the Bulgarian Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Bulgaria with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Bulgaria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-bulgaria#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Bulgaria guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/36/bulgaria#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Bulgaria","https://customs.bg/wps/portal/agency-en/home/info-citizens/Important%20notice%20for%20travelers"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food and drink into Bulgaria"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Bulgaria"]},{"k":"p","s":["As of 1 January 2026, the currency of Bulgaria will be the euro. Bulgarian lev will still be accepted until 31 January, but can be exchanged for euros free of charge at Bulgarian banks until 30 June 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["There may be some temporary disruption to card payments and to cash withdrawals from ATMs around 31 December 2025 to 1 January 2026 due to the changeover in currency. Cash payments will be unaffected."]},{"k":"p","s":["Major credit and debit cards are accepted in most banks and hotels. Most ATMs accept standard international credit and debit cards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pounds sterling and US dollars are easily exchanged for euros. Only exchange money at reliable places such as banks and currency exchange bureaux."]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare ",["cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more","https://customs.bg/wps/portal/agency-en/home/info-citizens/Carrying%20of%20cash,%20precious%20metals,%20gems%20and%20items%20containing%20them%20or%20made%20of%20them"],". You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Bulgaria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Bulgaria, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Protests and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasional political protests in towns and cities across Bulgaria. They can cause disruption to transport as protestors or police may set up roadblocks. Most protests are peaceful but there have been occasional incidents of violence, including by the police. Avoid all protests and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take sensible precautions to protect yourself from street crime, particularly in larger cities and late at night. Beware of any attempts to distract you. Watch out for pickpockets and bag thefts in tourist areas, on buses and trains and major public transport hubs, including airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Thefts from unattended cars at petrol stations have increased. Lock your car when going inside the petrol station to pay for your fuel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists are targeted by thieves and pickpockets in Sunny Beach and other larger cities and resorts. Thefts on the bus from Nessebar to Sunny Beach have also increased. Do not take valuables to the beach and be wary of poorly lit roads around the resort at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some tourists have been the victims of overcharging in so-called ‘gentlemen’s clubs’ in Sofia and in some resorts including Bansko, Borovets and Sunny Beach. Overcharging can amount to hundreds of pounds. Victims can be threatened with violence if they refuse to pay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get recommendations for bars and clubs from your hotel or other holidaymakers. When paying by card make sure the transaction is completed in your presence and be wary if asked to re-enter your PIN."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Thefts from accommodation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been burglaries from hotel rooms in Sunny Beach. Make sure you lock your room (including windows and balcony doors) and keep valuables locked in a safe."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been break-ins at properties in the residential areas of cities, and rural areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Thefts from cars"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may puncture your tyres or flag down your car. When you get out, the thieves can distract you and steal from your vehicle. Make sure the boot is locked and your luggage is secure."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Property fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Buyers have been defrauded while buying property. Be cautious and get legal advice before you buy. Only deal with established and reputable real estate agents or with other contacts who you know to be reliable and genuine."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["more details about buying property","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-bulgaria#accommodation-and-buying-property"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry ID. A printed copy of the photo page of your passport is acceptable."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and sex offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Bulgarian authorities treat all drug-related and sex offences very seriously. Any foreign nationals convicted of such offences can expect a prison sentence. Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using, or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Bulgaria have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drunken and disorderly behaviour"]},{"k":"p","s":["Offences relating to drunken, disorderly behaviour and hooliganism may be treated more seriously than in the UK. Police can arrest or fine anyone for loud and boisterous behaviour or urination in public places."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Football matches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crowd control measures and stewarding can be different from the UK and there have been a small number of incidents where ‘throwdown fireworks’ such as firecrackers or bangers have been set off in stadiums, risking injuries. Stay aware of your surroundings and be alert in crowded venues."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and binoculars in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid taking photographs near potentially sensitive areas like military establishments. If in doubt, ask permission."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Working with migrants in border regions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Assisting people who have entered Bulgaria illegally, or who are passing through Bulgaria to claim asylum in another country, risks breaking Bulgarian laws. It makes no difference whether you are helping them for profit or not – you are still at risk of breaking Bulgarian law. You can be arrested, detained and charged if you are suspected of facilitating illegal entry or stay in Bulgaria, including by helping with accommodation or transport. If you travel to Bulgaria to support civil society organisations working with migrants, seek advice from local expert organisations such as the ",["IOM","https://bulgaria.iom.int/"],", ",["UNHCR","https://www.unhcr.org/countries/bulgaria"]," or ",["Bulgarian Helsinki Committee","https://www.bghelsinki.org/en"]," to make sure that your proposed actions do not break Bulgarian laws."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Race-related incidents"]},{"k":"p","s":["The majority of visitors experience no difficulties related to their race, ethnicity or religious beliefs. However there have been a small number of verbal and physical attacks against ethnic minority UK nationals, including residents, in Bulgaria, and others have experienced unwanted attention or harassment in public places."]},{"k":"p","s":["Instances have increased at times of demonstrations organised by groups connected to populist or right-wing movements. Avoid all protests and stay aware of your surroundings, particularly when travelling alone or at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not illegal, but public attitudes are less tolerant than in the UK and the LGBT+ community generally keeps a low profile."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are a few gay bars and clubs in Sofia. The city also holds the annual Sofia Pride. Sofia Pride is growing in popularity and was attended in recent years by over 10,000 people. However, it attracts some negative attention locally and is held with a heightened police presence and security measures. If you want to join the parade, read the organisers’ Sofia Pride safety rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["In recent years, some verbal abuse and threatening behaviour was directed at people attending events related to Sofia Pride, including foreign visitors. You can report any hate crime to the organisers and the local police."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attitudes outside Sofia tend to be more conservative. There have been isolated cases of hostility towards people perceived to be from LGBT+ communities reported in Burgas and Plovdiv. You can find local information on LGBT+ issues in Bulgaria on the website of the ",["Bulgarian Helsinki Committee","https://www.bghelsinki.org/en/themes/lgbti"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Face-covering ban"]},{"k":"p","s":["Covering your face with a niqab, burka or similar head covering in public places is illegal in Bulgaria and police could give you a fine. This applies in public buildings, streets, parks, restaurants, shops and on public transport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sports activities like skiing, potholing and mountaineering, and sports classed as particularly dangerous – mountain biking, climbing, paragliding or BASE jumping – all carry risks. Your insurance should include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["mountain rescue services"]},{"k":"li","s":["helicopter costs"]},{"k":"li","s":["repatriation to your home country or possible transfer to neighbouring countries for treatment"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s more ",["information about mountain insurance","https://en.redcross.bg/activities/activities2"]," on the Bulgarian Red Cross website."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Quad biking and motorbikes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Quad biking is an extreme sport and carries the risk of serious injury or death. You need specific travel insurance to cover quad biking. Always read the details of your insurance cover, especially the small print and exclusions on your policy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you are given full instructions and training before your activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Insurance sold by the hire company usually only provides third-party insurance. It’s likely you will be charged for any damage to the rental vehicle and you may face arrest if you do not pay."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you hire a motorbike, you need a full motorbike licence. Make sure the vehicle is in good condition. Drivers and passengers must wear helmets. Failure to do so may invalidate your insurance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming and water sports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Obey any warning signs at coastal areas and beaches. Follow instructions from lifeguards and observe the flag indicators if they are present. Follow local advice if jellyfish or sea urchins are present."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more advice, see ",["Water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"p","s":["Book activities at a licensed water sports centre and before you start:"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure the paperwork is completed"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask for a safety demonstration"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you know how to call for help"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ⁠ ",["watersports safety advice","https://www.rospa.com/leisure-water-safety/water/advice/watersports-abroad"]," from the Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents (ROSPA)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Winter sports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read advice about ",["preparing for winter sports abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/winter-sports-stay-safe-on-the-slopes"],". The Bulgarian Mountain Rescue service publishes ",["safety rules on the ski slopes","https://www.pss-bg.bg/pravila-za-bezopasnost-po-ski-pistite/"]," (in Bulgarian)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avalanches are a risk in some areas. Always check the local snow and weather conditions if you plan to ski off-piste, and ski with a guide. There’s more information about avalanche risk from the ",["Bulgarian Mountain Rescue Service","https://www.pss-bg.bg/"]," (in Bulgarian)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to drive in Bulgaria, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Bulgaria guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/bulgaria/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you bring your own car to Bulgaria, you must have:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your driving licence"]},{"k":"li","s":["all original registration and ownership documents"]},{"k":"li","s":["proof of insurance that is valid in Bulgaria – although you are not required to have a green card to drive in Bulgaria, you may need it in some neighbouring countries"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If it’s a hired car, you must keep the contract document. Border officials will impound your vehicle if they are not satisfied that you own it or have permission to use it in Bulgaria."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vehicles that are registered outside the EU are considered to be ‘temporarily imported’ when driven inside Bulgaria. If your car is stolen in Bulgaria, you will be liable for import duty and related taxes."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["driving requirements if you live in Bulgaria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-bulgaria#driving-in-bulgaria"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions can be dangerous. Take care when driving, particularly at night and outside major cities. Many roads (and pavements) are in poor repair and roadworks are often unmarked and unlit at night. Driving standards are generally poor, and drivers can be aggressive, particularly on motorways. Avoid confrontations."]},{"k":"p","s":["There may be slow-moving cars and animal-drawn vehicles on the roads, particularly in rural areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must drive with side lights or dipped headlights, even during the daytime. Keep to the speed limit and make sure your vehicle is roadworthy. Traffic police issue on-the-spot fines for minor violations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bulgaria has strict penalties for driving under the influence of alcohol and drugs, and doing so could lead to vehicle confiscation, a prison sentence and fines. If you receive a penalty and do not own the vehicle, you could be required to pay a fine equivalent to the vehicle’s value."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tolls"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to use motorways and main roads outside towns, you’ll need to buy a digital vignette in advance of your journey. The vignette is a form of toll. If you use the roads without a vignette, traffic police will issue a fine. You can ",["buy a vignette online","https://www.tolltickets.com/en/country/bulgarien/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxis may not be in very good condition. Avoid taxis parked outside hotels or in tourist areas. Ask your hotel to call a taxi or flag down a passing taxi with a green ‘available’ light in the window. Check the licence sticker and the tariffs on the window before getting in as costs can vary considerably. Licensed taxis run by ‘Yellow’ operators are the most reliable."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular reports of robberies and threatening behaviour by taxi drivers in Sunny Beach. Use a taxi recommended by your tour operator or accommodation provider."]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in unlicensed taxis from Sofia airport overcharging passengers. If you’re travelling from the airport, make sure you take an official, licensed taxi. There is an ",["official taxi booking office","https://sofia-airport.eu/en/access/transportation/#by-taxi"]," in the arrivals hall. Check that the taxi meter is working before starting your journey."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail and bus travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thieves operate on trains. Make sure that documents and valuables are safe. The train system is very poor by European standards. There have been several fires on Bulgarian trains. Bulgaria has a comprehensive rail network, but trains can be cancelled at short notice. For travel updates see the ",["Bulgaria Railways website","https://www.bdz.bg/en"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The roadworthiness of vehicles and driving standards are not always good, and there have been a number of serious accidents in recent years."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["In summer and early autumn, Bulgaria is on a regular alert for wildfires. There is danger of large-scale and quick-spreading fires in forests and fields. Follow media reports and the advice of local authorities if wildfires occur in your area."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many parts of Bulgaria flood following heavy rains. Flooding is usually localised but can occasionally be widespread and has caused deaths. Watch for weather warnings on the National Institute of Meteorology and Hydrology website."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are earthquakes and small tremors throughout the year, usually without serious consequences. The last significant earthquakes were in 1928."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Bulgaria","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/36/bulgaria#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Bulgaria","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/36/bulgaria"],", including biting insects and ticks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Bulgaria. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Stray dogs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stray dogs are common and can be dangerous. Avoid getting too close to dogs, especially if they are in a pack. Take any animal bites seriously and seek immediate medical advice as rabies and other animal-borne diseases are present in Bulgaria."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Bulgaria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Bulgaria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bulgaria-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most Bulgarian hospitals are basic and old-fashioned compared to those in the UK. Standards of medical care are generally good, but specialised equipment and treatment may not be available. Hospital staff rarely speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Private clinics and hospitals are generally well-equipped and not expensive in comparison with the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign tourists have sometimes been overcharged in private clinics in tourist resorts. Hotels or resorts may call private ambulances. If you use private medical services, agree a price in advance. Ask whether there is a suitable public health facility nearby if you want to use a health insurance card, as these are not accepted by many private hospitals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Bulgaria, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["healthcare if you live in Bulgaria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-bulgaria"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Bulgaria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?country=Bulgaria&serviceType=lawyers"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?country=Bulgaria&serviceType=funeralDirectors"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?country=Bulgaria&serviceType=translatorsInterpreters"]," in Bulgaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Bulgaria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-bulgaria"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Bulgaria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bulgaria-prisoner-pack/information-pack-for-british-nationals-detained-or-imprisoned-in-bulgaria"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/bulgaria/british-embassy-sofia"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bulgaria/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Bulgaria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-bulgaria"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":26362,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brunei":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"c83b995c0aa72fa4e40415d9635d83be18c38aba15f748c0e7828edd0044d4ae","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/brunei","bytes":52861,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Brunei travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2012-12-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-19T14:05:48+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brunei/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Brunei’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Brunei set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Brunei High Commission in the UK","https://www.mfa.gov.bn/uk-london/SitePages/Home.aspx"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Brunei, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive. It must not be damaged or have any pages missing. If your passport does not meet these conditions, you may be refused entry and detained."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a dual national, you should use the same passport to enter and exit Brunei. The passport you use for entry will determine your nationality in Brunei."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Brunei dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Brunei does not recognise the dual nationality of Bruneians. The immigration authorities can refuse your entry if you hold a Bruneian passport and a passport of a different nationality."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter on a Brunei passport, you cannot access British consular assistance, as you will be treated as a Bruneian national."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["British citizen passport holders may enter Brunei as visitors for up to 90 days without a visa. If you have another type of British nationality, check visa requirements with Brunei immigration authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer or if you’re travelling for work, study, business travel or other reasons, you must meet the Brunei government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Brunei High Commission in the UK","https://www.mfa.gov.bn/uk-london/SitePages/Home.aspx"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped when you enter Brunei."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Overstaying your visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not overstay your visa or violate the terms of entry. Penalties include detention and caning."]},{"k":"h","s":["Declaration form"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must ",["submit an e-arrival declaration form","https://www.imm.gov.bn/"]," to enter Brunei. Do this before you travel as it may be requested at check-in. You do not need to complete the arrival form if you are not passing through immigration."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must also complete the ",["Health Declaration Form","https://www.healthinfo.gov.bn/travel#/user/login"]," before or upon arrival. More information can be found at the ",["Ministry of Health website","https://www.moh.gov.bn/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Land and sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check ",["border post opening hours","https://www.immigration.gov.bn/SitePages/Pos-Pos%20Kawalan.aspx"]," before you travel. They are not open 24 hours. Make sure your exit and entry stamps are correct before leaving the border post."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Brunei, you must have certificates to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]]},{"k":"li","s":["a polio vaccine, in some circumstances"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Brunei guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/35/brunei#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods and the amount of alcohol you can take into and out of Brunei","https://bdnsw.mofe.gov.bn/Pages/ImpExpProh-RestictionGoods.aspx"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can complete a declaration through the Customs.BN app or on arrival at the airport. Download the app for ",["Android","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=rced.egnc.customsbn&pli=1https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=rced.egnc.customsbn&pli=1"]," or ",["iOS","https://apps.apple.com/us/app/customs-bn/id6449696019"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Brunei"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Brunei, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low, but there are occasional incidents of petty crime against tourists as well as house burglaries. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care of your passport"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying valuables with you"]},{"k":"li","s":["not leave possessions in unattended vehicles, even if out of sight"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Islam is the official religion in Brunei. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions. Make sure that your actions do not cause offence, especially during the holy month of Ramadan. There may be serious penalties for doing something that might not be illegal in the UK but is in Brunei."]},{"k":"p","s":["Places of business and offices, including shops and restaurants, shut between midday and 2pm every Friday for prayers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Friday is a non-working day for government offices and local schools. Government offices and state schools open on Saturdays instead."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, it is against the law to be seen eating or drinking in public during fasting hours. You must also not smoke in public."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should dress modestly. For example, do not wear shorts in government and public buildings such as health centres."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criticism of the Bruneian Royal Family"]},{"k":"p","s":["His Majesty The Sultan and other members of the Bruneian Royal Family are highly revered and public criticism of them causes great offence and may result in legal action."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Relationships outside marriage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Adultery and closeness in private between an unmarried man and woman is illegal if one person is a Muslim. In general, public displays of affection may cause offence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pornographic material"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession of pornographic material is illegal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Firearms, ammunition and explosives"]},{"k":"p","s":["Brunei has very strict laws against the possession of firearms, blank or live ammunition and explosives, including fireworks and firecrackers. Do not carry these items or replicas into Brunei."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Brunei criminalises same-sex sexual activity. Sentences include a maximum penalty of death by stoning, whipping, imprisonment and fines. However there is currently a moratorium on the death penalty and there is limited evidence of same-sex activity laws being implemented in recent years. The gender expression of trans people is also criminalised and this law is occasionally enforced with fines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for drug offences in Brunei including, in some cases, the death penalty. Other crimes may be punished by caning and lengthy prison sentences."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["The sale of alcohol and tobacco in Brunei is illegal. Non-Muslims aged 17 and over may import a limited amount of alcohol. This must be declared to the customs authorities on arrival and drunk in private."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Smoking is illegal in certain public places, including shopping and eating areas, bus stops and stations, car parks and in close proximity to any public buildings."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police advise against hiking alone in the forest, including at well-known recreation areas. It’s easy to get lost when visiting the rainforest. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["use recognised and well-known guides"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay on paths and trails, rather than pushing through the undergrowth"]},{"k":"li","s":["always carry food and water with you"]},{"k":"li","s":["consider carrying a whistle to attract attention and a torch"]},{"k":"li","s":["wear closed-toe shoes"]},{"k":"h","s":["Wildlife"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Saltwater crocodiles"]},{"k":"p","s":["Saltwater crocodiles have attacked and killed people fishing on riverbanks around Bandar. Crocodiles have also been seen on beaches and in the ponds of the Panaga golf course. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["pay attention to signs warning of crocodiles"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from the water’s edge"]},{"k":"li","s":["seek local advice on taking further precautions"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Venomous snakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are a number of venomous snakes in Brunei. If you see a snake while outdoors:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your distance"]},{"k":"li","s":["wait for the snake to move away"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you find a snake indoors or outside in a confined space, like a garden, call the fire service (‘bomba’) on 995."]},{"k":"p","s":["The RIPAS public hospital in Bandar Seri Begawan carries antivenom. Get medical advice if a snake bites you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Brunei, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Brunei with a valid UK driving licence for up to 90 days. You’ll then need to ",["apply for a Bruneian licence from the Land Transport Department","https://www.jpd.gov.bn/SitePages/Land%20Transport%20Department/Services/Driving%20Licenses.aspx"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If your vehicle is not registered in Brunei, you can only buy motor fuel at ",["14 designated filling stations","https://bsm.com.bn/products/shell-fuels/shell-v-power/"],", to a maximum of 250 litres. Petrol stations will only sell premium “V-Power” fuel to foreign cars. You can usually only pay in cash."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re driving to Malaysia with a Bruneian registered car, the same is true – foreign registered vehicles are only permitted to buy premium RON97 fuel (not the subsidised RON95 fuel) and this is not available in all petrol stations. Make sure to fill up before leaving a city."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are different from the UK. Vehicles do not always stop at red lights or pedestrian crossings. It is common for drivers not to use seatbelts or child car seats and to speed. Road surfaces are uneven and accidents are common. Animals such as monitor lizards, snakes and monkeys could be on the roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re involved in a road accident as a driver, do not leave the scene or move the vehicle until the police arrive (call 993 for the police)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Small boats carry passengers across to the water village in Bandar and along the rivers on cruises. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check there are adequate life jackets for all passengers, including children"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep hands inside the boat, as there may be river crocodiles"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re taking a longer trip, for example, a wildlife cruise, get local recommendations and plan your trip in advance."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have an existing health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 991 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Brunei","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/35/brunei#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Brunei","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/35/brunei"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most branded pharmaceuticals are readily available, though some items available without a prescription in the UK may need a doctor’s prescription in Brunei."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Brunei"]},{"k":"p","s":["Standards of healthcare in Brunei are generally acceptable, though basic hospital supplies can occasionally run low. There are 2 significant medical facilities, the Government General Hospital (RIPAS) in Bandar Seri Begawan and the private Jerudong Park Medical Centre (JPMC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need medical evacuation to Singapore if there are complications. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Brunei","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/brunei-list-of-medical-facilities-and-practitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read the ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Brunei"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 991"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 995"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 993"]},{"k":"p","s":["Search and rescue: 998"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers in Brunei","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=brunei"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Brunei","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-pack-brunei"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Brunei","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/brunei-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/brunei/british-high-commission-bandar-seri-begawan"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brunei/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Brunei","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-brunei"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":15161,"change":"Updated information about global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/5-ontario-education-unions-hold-strike-votes-as-cuts-squeeze-classrooms-294338":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"e714743df150e97e2b778eaae6ba04671129e87f95064aca360f836697e93cfd","read":"https://theconversation.com/5-ontario-education-unions-hold-strike-votes-as-cuts-squeeze-classrooms-294338","bytes":188382,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"5 Ontario education unions hold strike votes as cuts squeeze classrooms","by":[{"n":"Chantal Mancini","r":"Adjunct Assistant Professor of Labour Studies, McMaster University"}],"pub":"2026-10-29T14:52:00Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Five major unions representing Ontario education workers will hold ",["strike votes in November","https://nowtoronto.com/news/ontario-education-unions-strike-votes-november-2026/"],". Their contracts expired Aug. 31, 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["The move signals a potential showdown with Premier Doug Ford’s Conservative government after many months of warnings about deteriorating learning and working conditions in the province’s schools. As both a labour studies scholar and a secondary teacher, I am uniquely positioned to provide the context."]},{"k":"p","s":["Strike votes do not necessarily mean that workers will walk off the job. In fact, ",["95 per cent of labour disputes in Canada are resolved without a strike","https://www.pearson.com/en-ca/subject-catalog/p/labour-relations/P200000010237?view=educator"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unions use strike votes as a pressure tactic to signal to employers ",["that workers are united in their cause","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/toronto/queens-park-teachers-rally-public-education-9.7394914"],". The co-ordination of the unions’ votes is a clear message to the government that they’re prepared to collectively pursue their goals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Why are unions now sending this message? The current stall in negotiations follows the ",["provincial government’s indication to unions that it wants greater control over negotiating issues","https://www.etfo.ca/news-publications/media-releases/joint-statement-calandras-bargaining-bluster-falls-flat"],", such as staffing timelines related to transfer, surplus and redundancy, as well as professional development funding ",["and contracting out.","https://www.cambridgetoday.ca/local-news/unions-criticize-outsourcing-of-custodial-staff-at-new-cambridge-joint-use-school-12752246"]]},{"k":"p","s":["This comes ",["as unions say","https://www.instagram.com/p/DcThI0slh1_/"]," classrooms are under severe strain driven by the government’s chronic ",["underfunding of education","https://www.thestar.com/politics/ontario-s-education-funding-per-student-is-decreasing-after-inflation-watchdog-finds/article_aa8b1bab-cf4a-439a-9b9a-a8d2881e5589.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Greater control over staffing?"]},{"k":"p","s":["A move towards greater government control over staffing would fall in line with the Ministry of Education’s centralization of power, following a ",["provincial takeover of eight school boards","https://globalnews.ca/news/11717907/york-catholic-district-school-takeover/"]," and ",["restrictions on the power of elected trustees","https://www.thetrillium.ca/news/education-and-training/breaking-ford-government-to-restrict-number-and-duties-of-school-board-trustees-12134818"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unions know that ",["exerting greater control over costs via centralization can be translated into additional cuts","https://doi.org/10.18740/S4TC7R"]," (and more underfunding and erosion of working and learning conditions)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Centralization also cuts out democratic input by local workers and their unions (and parents and trustees)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Attacks on school boards threaten local democracy","https://theconversation.com/attacks-on-school-boards-threaten-local-democracy-261895"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Staffing cuts, lack of resources"]},{"k":"p","s":["Education workers are ",["facing significant staffing cuts","https://www.ctvnews.ca/video/2026/10/09/education-other-public-service-workers-saw-the-brunt-of-job-cuts-in-september/"],". Teachers are increasingly faced with larger ",["classes of students","https://www.etfo.ca/news-publications/media-releases/etfo-bringing-class-size-fight-to-bargaining-table"]," with ",["diverse learning and behavioural needs","https://www.ctf-fce.ca/class-size-isnt-the-whole-story/"]," they say they are unable to meet."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Canadian Teachers’ Federation notes that across provinces, teachers say students who need help aren’t getting it and teaching time is being lost as a result: Teachers in ",["Québec,","https://theconversation.com/quebecs-teacher-strike-offers-lessons-on-the-urgent-need-to-support-public-education-220363"]," ",["Saskatchewan","https://theconversation.com/saskatchewan-teacher-strike-its-about-bargaining-for-the-common-good-221095"]," and ",["Alberta","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/calgary/classroom-complexity-teacher-voices-9.7099882"]," made the same point in recent bargaining."]},{"k":"p","s":["Reports point to ",["rising school violence and burnout","https://www.thestar.com/news/ontario/violence-harassment-and-burnout-ontarios-education-workers-are-in-crisis-study-finds/article_ac79b129-d6e0-4d93-a2fc-9bac94912c58.html"]," driven by a lack of resources and supports. ",["Ministry of Education data","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/toronto/ontario-teacher-shortage-ministry-of-educaiton-1.7339837"]," warns of a teacher recruitment and retention problem expected to worsen by 2027."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["To improve literacy, Ontario should invest in students and educators","https://theconversation.com/to-improve-literacy-ontario-should-invest-in-students-and-educators-280758"]]},{"k":"p","s":[["Educational assistants","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/toronto/ea-shortage-ontario-9.7268522"]," are in short supply, making the situation particularly difficult for ",["students with special learning needs","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/toronto/ontario-auditor-general-report-education-9.7196608"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Education unions say ",["education workers have had enough.","https://underfunded.ca/"]," The Ford government says it’s made ",["record investments in education,","https://paulcalandra.com/ontario-making-record-investments-to-put-student-achievement-first/"]," but ",["research estimates","https://www.policyalternatives.ca/news-research/ontario-school-funding-shortfall-continues-to-grow-reaching-6-4-billion-since-2018/"]," a $6.5-billion-dollar shortfall in the system since the Conservatives came to power in 2018."]},{"k":"p","s":["With ",["school boards posting record deficits","https://globalnews.ca/news/11955405/ontario-supervisor-deficits/"],", students are ",["losing programs","https://www.thetrillium.ca/news/education-and-training/an-unmitigated-disaster-for-students-outcry-grows-over-education-cuts-outside-tdsb-headquarters-ahead-of-delayed-parent-advisory-meeting-12399438"]," and ",["schools are in a state of disrepair","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/toronto/ontario-fao-school-repair-construction-shortfall-1.7412722"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ontario teachers and other education workers (like educational assistants, early childhood educators, speech language pathologists, school psychologists, school custodians, office administrators) are represented by multiple unions. These unions will need to demonstrate unprecedented solidarity if they hope to achieve the funding improvements and retain local control over bargaining staffing and contracting out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Local bargaining matters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Education unions in the province must follow a specific negotiations process set out in the ",["School Boards Collective Bargaining Act","https://www.ontario.ca/laws/statute/14s05"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The act was passed by ",["the Liberals in 2014","https://news.ontario.ca/en/release/29016/ontario-strengthening-education-sector-for-students"],", and can be understood as part of an ",["overall trend towards province-wide negotiations","https://www.saskoer.ca/understandingcanadianschools/chapter/9-7-collective-bargaining/"]," across Canada."]},{"k":"p","s":["This legislation transformed education bargaining. It required that each union, at their own bargaining table with the government, must agree to which things will be bargained “centrally” with the government, and which items will be bargained “locally” with the school boards before any actual negotiations take place."]},{"k":"p","s":["Normally, ",["central issues bargained with the government","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/toronto/ontario-teachers-unions-labour-negotiations-9.7327115"]," consist of high-cost items such wages, benefits and sick leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["Preserving local bargaining over staffing matters for educators because teachers and support staff have different needs. Each school board, and corresponding local union, will have issues that are unique to their community."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take, for example, staff transfers: In a school board area serving Hamilton, Ont., transferring a teacher from one school to another might seem more workable because the distance between the two most outlying schools is ",["arguably not that long of a drive","https://www.hwdsb.on.ca/school-boundary-maps"],". In a northern school board, or even in the Toronto District School Board serving the greater Toronto area, a transfer could mean relocating your family due to the distance or the commute."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unions have sent the disputes over what must be negotiated with the province and what must be negotiated with school boards ",["to the Ontario Labour Relations Board","https://www.thoroldtoday.ca/local-news/elementary-teachers-contract-talks-on-hold-over-dispute-that-could-stretch-into-school-year-12622662#google_vignette"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hearings ",["are concluding","https://www.innisfiltoday.ca/local-news/ontario-education-unions-ramp-up-strike-preparations-as-bargaining-remains-stalled-12809519"],", with a decision expected weeks later. The timing will likely coincide with the unions’ strike vote results."]},{"k":"h","s":["How would a job action proceed?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Unions would need to demonstrate a majority of members voting yes for any job action to proceed."]},{"k":"p","s":["The parties must first engage in a period of meaningful bargaining and other mandatory ",["labour relations processes","https://osstftoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/EN-Barganing-Process-chart.pdf"]," before any work-to-rule, strike or lockout can occur."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unions must provide five days’ written notice before engaging in job action. School boards must provide the same notice before locking out workers."]},{"k":"h","s":["Gearing up for conflict?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Like ",["earlier governments","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/toronto/liberals-strike-historic-wage-freeze-deal-with-catholic-teachers-1.1185659"],", the Ford government has proven it will resort to ",["divide-and-conquer strategies","https://globalnews.ca/news/9923475/ontario-teachers-union-strike-education-minister/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2022, only weeks after education contracts expired, the premier ",["removed CUPE education workers’ right to strike","https://breachmedia.ca/the-inside-story-of-how-education-workers-beat-back-doug-ford/"]," by invoking the notwithstanding clause."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was not until ",["other unions threatened a general strike","https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/article-ford-cupe-notwithstanding-canadian-unions/"]," that he backed down."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ontario school strike: Government’s use of the notwithstanding clause — again — is an assault on labour relations","https://theconversation.com/ontario-school-strike-governments-use-of-the-notwithstanding-clause-again-is-an-assault-on-labour-relations-193824"]]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s clear this time that the government is gearing up for conflict once again. Just before contracts expired, a ",["media report","https://www.thetrillium.ca/news/education-and-training/ford-government-preparing-education-ads-taking-aim-at-teacher-unions-as-contract-talks-grind-to-a-halt-leaked-script-12674031"]," leaked the government’s plan for an ad campaign taking aim at education workers’ use of sick leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["The complex nature of collective bargaining in the education sector makes this round’s outcome tough to predict."]},{"k":"p","s":["Education unions — particularly those who represent teachers — tend to favour work-to-rule campaigns and rotating strikes over total walkouts. They are mindful of both ",["public opinion","https://www.ctvnews.ca/ottawa/article/ontarians-express-support-for-cupe-as-education-workers-strike-continues-poll-finds/"]," and the threat of ",["back-to-work legislation","https://www.tvo.org/article/ontario-forces-teachers-back-to-work-here-responses-from-across-the-province"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, CUPE has indicated that this time around, ",["it will escalate quickly to a strike if necessary.","https://www.thestar.com/politics/provincial/forget-work-to-rule-school-support-staff-will-go-straight-to-strike-if-necessary-union-says/article_933da333-b747-42c7-a504-69280ed8f242.html"]," Whether the rest of the ",["255,000 education workers in the province","https://www.etfo.ca/news-publications/media-releases/ontario-education-unions-serve-notice-to-bargain-2026"]," would join them remains to be seen."]},{"k":"p","s":["What this fight will look like will be determined in the weeks ahead. Clearly, there is much at stake."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is an updated version of a story originally published on Oct. 29, 2026. It clarifies that the author is both a labour studies scholar and a secondary teacher."]}],"chars":7193},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/macao":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"03a5f35b2ffd23f3e3b69966f17eefdb4998e2b627ba4d97e1d758a771741172","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/macao","bytes":45637,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Macao (SAR of China) travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2012-12-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-11T11:32:17+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers the Macao Special Administrative Region (SAR). For mainland China, see ",["travel advice for China","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/china"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual Chinese-British nationality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Macao does not recognise dual nationality. If you have both British and Chinese nationality, the local authorities may treat you as a Chinese citizen, even if you enter Macao on a full “British citizen” passport. If this is the case, the British Consulate-General may not be able to offer you consular help."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have formally renounced Chinese citizenship, carry evidence that you have done so."]},{"k":"p","s":["See guidance on ",["nationality in China","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nationality-in-china"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/macao/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Macao’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Macao set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Chinese Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 90 days after the date you leave Macao."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other types of ",["British nationals who are exempt from ETA","https://www.gov.uk/eta/when-not-need-eta"]," must also carry a valid British passport when entering the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Macao is part of the People’s Republic of China, but it remains a Special Administrative Region (SAR) with its own immigration controls."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Macao for up to 6 months without a visa, for tourism and to undertake unpaid business activities."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, to do paid work, to study, or for other reasons, you must get a visa before arrival. Check which type of visa you need with the ",["Macao Immigration Department","https://www.macaotourism.gov.mo/en/travelessential/before-you-travel/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling through Macao to China"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to travel through Macao to mainland China on a British passport, you must get a Chinese visa before you arrive at the border. If not, you could be fined or detained by the mainland Chinese authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter and leave Macao through mainland China, you must get a double or multiple entry visa to re-enter mainland China."]},{"k":"p","s":["The mainland Chinese authorities may carry out thorough checks at border crossings, including of your electronic devices."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Macao, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Macao guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/50/chinamacao#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Accommodation"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must stay in licensed accommodation. You could be fined up to 3,000 Macanese pataca (about £300) if you stay in illegal accommodation. Find accommodation or check your accommodation is licensed on the ",["Macao Tourism Office","https://www.macaotourism.gov.mo/en/accommodation/"]," website."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Macao. You must ",["declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty","https://www.macaotourism.gov.mo/en/travelessential/before-you-travel/entry-requirements?tab=customs"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Macao airport has a ",["passenger guide","https://www.macau-airport.com/en/passenger-guide/arrival"]," that explains the allowances."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Macao"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Macao, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low but pickpocketing and other street crime does happen. You should take particular care of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["passports, credit cards and money in crowded areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["your belongings when checking out of hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["your wallet and other valuables when visiting casinos late at night"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Safeguarding National Security Law"]},{"k":"p","s":["You could face criminal charges if you take part in activities that the authorities believe threaten national security. This includes activities in and outside the Macao SAR, including in the UK. The Safeguarding National Security Law (NSL) outlines the types of activities that are illegal, such as preparing for or carrying out treason, secession or subversion against the central government."]},{"k":"p","s":["The police have the right to access an individual’s social media and private communications to gather evidence of NSL crimes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not become involved with drugs. Possession of drugs can lead to imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking photos in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take photos of military installations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Macao, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Macao with a Hong Kong, Chinese or Portuguese driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are using a UK driving licence, you need a ",["1949 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will also need to ",["register to drive in Macao for more than 14 days","https://www.gov.mo/en/services/ps-1488/ps-1488a/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Car hire"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some car hire companies have additional requirements, such as at least a year of driving experience and a minimum age of 21."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Unlicensed taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Uber is illegal in Macao. The Macao police will take action against drivers and passengers of unlicensed taxi services, including Uber."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Typhoons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Typhoon season normally runs from May to November. Typhoons very occasionally hit Macao and could cause flooding and landslides. Public offices will shut down when the ‘Typhoon 8’ signal is issued. Be aware of local warning signals issued in advance and follow advice issued by the local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor weather updates from the ",["World Meteorological Organization","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/wnp/index.html"]," and the ",["Macao Meteorological and Geophysical Bureau","https://www.smg.gov.mo/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Macao","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/50/chinamacao#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Macao","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/50/chinamacao"],", including malaria and dengue fever."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Prescriptions issued by UK doctors are not valid in Macao. You will need to see a local doctor to get a prescription."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Macao"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Macao","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/macao-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Macao"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Tourism Crisis Management Office"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact the Macao Tourism Crisis Management Office on (853) 2833 3000 (24-hour hotline) for immediate and general tourism advice in English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Macao"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Macao"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Macao"]," in Macao"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Macao","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-for-macao/macao-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being arrested or ",["imprisoned in Macao","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/macao-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/macao/british-consulate-general-hong-kong"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/macao/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Macao","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-macao"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":10355,"change":"New information about dual nationals returning to the UK (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/why-it-could-be-a-bad-idea-to-get-ai-to-flirt-for-you-295274":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"dfa0f8d8b426f5f243debfc9172315f0bcddfdd3ecbc76b64587f438947ca5d1","read":"https://theconversation.com/why-it-could-be-a-bad-idea-to-get-ai-to-flirt-for-you-295274","bytes":178991,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Why it could be a bad idea to get AI to flirt for you","by":[{"n":"Ten-Herng Lai","r":"Lecturer in Philosophy, University of Stirling"},{"n":"Alfred Archer","r":"Assistant Professor, School of Humanities and Digital Sciences, Tilburg University"}],"pub":"2026-10-30T12:26:58Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["You finally started an online conversation with a stranger you find attractive, yet you don’t really know what to say. They seem happy to talk, but you struggle to find the correct responses. You worry that their patience is growing thin. You pray for some guidance. Luckily, the solution could be just a few clicks away."]},{"k":"p","s":["After all, you have the power of ",["AI","https://theconversation.com/topics/artificial-intelligence-ai-90"]," at your fingertips. Why not use it to come up with something fun and interesting to say?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet many of us might hesitate in this scenario. Researchers have already warned of ",["“cognitive debt”","https://www.media.mit.edu/publications/your-brain-on-chatgpt/"]," – students can use AI to write excellent assignments, but then ",["fail miserably","https://cepr.org/publications/dp21577"]," in final exams because they remember nothing. No one would want to show up to a date unable to recall anything they had copied and pasted into an online conversation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flirting online, like many other emotionally loaded tasks such as writing an apology, a eulogy or a message of congratulations, reflects how you feel about the person. The philosopher ",["Talbot Brewer","https://academic.oup.com/book/34596/chapter/294250266"]," wrote that a person’s efforts to make sense of their emotions through articulating them can reveal what they value."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, suppose someone thought she didn’t especially care about her work. But then she found herself feeling pride when she was promoted. Her emotion may reveal to her that she does in fact care about workplace success."]},{"k":"h","s":["How your emotions reveal yourself to you"]},{"k":"p","s":["In our ",["recent research","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s13347-026-01203-4"],", we contend that using AI to flirt – or for any other task where personal connection is valuable – risks bypassing those moments where emotions can reveal important self-knowledge."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perhaps in flirting online, a person may not read what their date says carefully. Instead, they might quickly copy the text into ChatGPT and then equally quickly paste the response back into the chat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alternatively, perhaps an AI wingman is already integrated into the dating app, allowing people to simply click and send the suggested text. They don’t pay attention to what the date says, maybe overlooking potential deal-breakers, things that might be odd, or small stylistic details that would otherwise give them some pause."]},{"k":"p","s":["By outsourcing this emotional task to ChatGPT, it’s possible for a person to deprive themselves of the opportunity to really let the moments affect them. They could miss the chance to properly consider whether they would be happy to make compromises for their date. They may not even know whether they are genuinely excited about the date."]},{"k":"p","s":["Instead of slowly articulating their feelings and, in so doing, working out what they value in a relationship, they are authorising AI to say whatever might impress their date."]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s also the issue of ",["privacy","https://www.ethicaldatingonline.com/open-letter"]," – the flirty exchanges could find their way into training data. And is the AI wingman even trustworthy? It could misrepresent the person using it – and the other party might feel they’d suffered a deception. Even before AI, researchers have questioned whether lying on dating platforms ",["invalidates consent","https://doi.org/10.1086/670249"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the end of the day, it just feels a bit disrespectful. The output of AI has little to do with how someone feels about their date, but ",["draws more from the training data","https://doi.org/10.1093/pq/pqag043"],". This data has nothing to do with the person or their date."]},{"k":"p","s":["But maybe some people are less careless. Plenty of daters would make sure to scrutinise the AI output before sending it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet humans have a tendency to overly trust AI. ",["Another study","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s13347-025-00932-2"]," found that when people regularly let AI produce their first draft, they tend to accept the output uncritically. The study also found that people can easily adopt the biases of large language models (LLMs), even if they know those biases exist."]},{"k":"p","s":["From our own study, one worry that emerged was that instead of being true to their own feelings, over-reliance on AI may give the LLMs too much say in shaping what a person values."]},{"k":"p","s":["We are not suggesting that people should never outsource emotional tasks to AI. Sometimes, there’s no other option but to interact with emotionally manipulative or difficult people – perhaps a relative or an ex-partner. If you are already certain about your feelings towards this person, it may be better to refuse to let them ",["get to you","https://www.theatlantic.com/family/2026/10/ai-family-text/688962/"],". AI may provide some breathing space."]},{"k":"p","s":["But if as humans we want to get to know other people, have or repair meaningful relations, or make sure that what we communicate truly reflects how we feel, we should consider resisting the temptation to outsource our emotions to AI. After all, our emotions have the power to reveal to us what we deeply value."]}],"chars":4471},"https://theconversation.com/thomas-markle-allegations-undo-years-of-media-attacks-painting-meghan-as-cold-and-callous-295333":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"2aa984a8cfebda3a00fdb68b2616b3c4588121453b004cb1d22626f173fd3df0","read":"https://theconversation.com/thomas-markle-allegations-undo-years-of-media-attacks-painting-meghan-as-cold-and-callous-295333","bytes":189105,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Thomas Markle allegations undo years of media attacks painting Meghan as cold and callous","by":[{"n":"Tiara Sukhan","r":"Assistant Professor, Faculty of Information & Media Studies, Western University"}],"pub":"2026-11-03T15:51:01Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["For years, British tabloid coverage invited readers to understand Meghan Markle’s estrangement from her father as yet another chapter in the ",["Meghan Markle saga","https://doi.org/10.1080/07491409.2021.1912516"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shame on the ",["uncaring daughter","https://www.news.com.au/entertainment/celebrity-life/royals/meghan-markle-slammed-for-dad-book-when-shes-estranged-from-her-own/news-story/060c4677f2491bead5dc0082eec334c0"]," who had abandoned her aging father and denied him access to his grandchildren. Meghan, the Duchess of Sussex, offered no explanation for the estrangement, leaving a gap for the media to fill with endless supposition and speculation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Now, however, readers are privy to both ",["facts and allegations that push back","https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/23/thomas-markle-sr-allegations-challenge-media-meghan-narrative?"]," on the narrative long established by publications like the Mirror, The Sun and the Daily Mail, the newspaper whose reporter, Caroline Graham, ",["developed a close, longstanding friendship with Thomas Markle","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cy47089ql14o"]," while writing frequently on his estrangement from his daughter."]},{"k":"p","s":["We now know that in ",["2019, British police gave the duchess a letter containing allegations","https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/30/iopc-watchdog-investigate-met-police-meghan-warning-letter"]," about her father."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meghan says that at the time, she had believed authorities were investigating the claims and that she ",["was told not to go public with them","https://people.com/meghan-markle-told-by-uk-police-not-to-speak-about-allegations-against-dad-thomas-markle-detailed-2019-letter-report-12206888"]," due to the potential legal implications. In her statement, she said her decision to keep her father away from her children ",["was about protecting them more than punishing him","https://globalnews.ca/news/12118338/meghan-markle-deeply-distressed-child-sex-abuse-image-claims-against-dad-thomas-markle/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The allegations of Thomas Markle’s criminal behaviour do not just ask us to reconsider Meghan’s actions. They ask us to reconsider the ",["media narrative","https://theconversation.com/whats-fuelling-the-medias-enduring-hate-campaign-against-meghan-markle-239906"]," through which we understood them."]},{"k":"h","s":["Thomas Markle’s media attacks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thomas Markle has been a recurring media presence since Prince Harry and Meghan’s 2018 wedding. His estrangement from his daughter quickly became a tabloid staple as he made himself readily available to media outlets, ",["and was reportedly paid to do so","https://www.news.com.au/entertainment/celebrity-life/royals/thomas-markle-was-paid-for-his-tellall-interview/news-story/c1de54f6c5b2b5fb2bab4448ef5911ae"]," — itself an ethical violation for most reputable news organizations."]},{"k":"p","s":["He gave interviews and ",["expressed how hurt he felt","https://www.dailymail.com/news/article-12030517/Meghan-teenage-homecoming-queen-Unseen-footage-duchess-shared-estranged-family.html"],". He talked about ",["not meeting his grandchildren","https://www.dailymail.com/news/article-12530379/Meghan-Markles-father-Thomas-Markle-wants-reconciliation.html"],". He supplied an ongoing story for a ravenous public already primed to take his side."]},{"k":"p","s":["Had the media prioritized journalistic objectivity and ethics, it should have become a problem that Thomas Markle would talk when Meghan would not."]},{"k":"p","s":["But withheld information does not stop a celebrity narrative; it just becomes part of the story."]},{"k":"p","s":["A clear informational asymmetry developed as the duchess’s apparent motivations were constructed on the basis of her silence in the face of her father’s verbosity. It should also be noted here that Prince Harry successfully launched a privacy lawsuit against the Mirror group of newspapers, settled with The Sun and lost against The Daily Mail — three news outlets that are among his wife’s harshest and most relentless critics."]},{"k":"p","s":["The British media didn’t simply report dispassionately on a family conflict between Thomas Markle and his daughter; it served up an unbalanced version of the conflict that many readers ate up."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meghan’s failure to reconcile was interpreted as callousness. Her unwillingness to explain herself was portrayed as evidence of an unappealing aloofness. Keeping her children from their grandfather was presented as proof of how vindictive or status-obsessed she was."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is of course also a narrative dependent upon culturally recognizable expectations about daughters, who are supposed to perform care, forgiveness, reconciliation and family obligation. Meghan’s refusal to behave as a dutiful daughter demanded an explanation, which ",["media commentators were happy to supply","https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2018/dec/17/its-no-surprise-thomas-markle-and-his-daughter-meghan-are-now-estranged"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The now-public allegations about Thomas Markle reveal how precarious those explanations always were, particularly given the nature of the personal relationship between Thomas Markle and Graham, the Daily Mail‘s embedded reporter. This makes the usual distinction between reporting a story and participating in its construction increasingly difficult to sustain."]},{"k":"h","s":["Embedded reporter"]},{"k":"p","s":["When Thomas Markle was hospitalized in 2025, ",["Meghan’s spokesperson cited the constant presence","https://news.sky.com/story/meghan-contacts-estranged-father-thomas-markle-in-philippines-hospital-13481717?"]," of Graham at his bedside as a barrier that made private contact with him virtually impossible."]},{"k":"p","s":[["DMG Media responded","https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/home-news/meghan-markle-letter-estranged-father-hospital-b2881740.html"]," that Graham had had a “close relationship” with Thomas Markle since 2018, that Markle had asked her to come to his bedside and that she didn’t report on anything without his consent."]},{"k":"p","s":["But this acknowledged closeness raises an important question. At what point does sustained access become participation in the family drama being reported?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Previously the Mail on Sunday ",["published Meghan’s private letter to her father, leading her to successfully sue the publication","https://doi.org/10.1177/09564748221083129"],". There is a pattern evident in the Mail’s behaviour as private communications between father and daughter repeatedly became public media content."]},{"k":"p","s":["These are familiar issues for the British media. The ",["Leveson Inquiry (2011-12)","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/leveson-inquiry-report-into-the-culture-practices-and-ethics-of-the-press"]," was established to investigate the culture, practices and ethics of the U.K. media after the ",["phone-hacking scandal","https://www.cnn.com/2013/10/24/world/europe/uk-phone-hacking-scandal-fast-facts"],". More than a decade later, the Thomas Markle story suggests that questions about the relationship between access, intrusion and public interest have hardly disappeared."]},{"k":"p","s":["Leveson was of course not the first time the media came under close scrutiny. The public outrage after the ",["death of Princess Diana","https://doi.org/10.1177/030981689806400104"]," in 1997 was largely directed at the photographers who were chasing her into a Paris tunnel that night and ",["the tabloid outlets that employed them","https://doi.org/10.1177/107769900308000311"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This prompted the industry’s self-regulatory body, the now-defunct Press Complaints Commission, to tighten its code of practice regarding harassment and privacy. Yet ultimately this regulatory framework failed to curb intrusive behaviour."]},{"k":"h","s":["The role of social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["For nearly 10 years, the media has been deploying aggressive tactics against the Duchess of Sussex that ",["mirror the harassment","https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/mar/08/harry-meghan-oprah-winfrey-royal-british-"]," faced by her late mother-in-law. But two key factors differentiate the experiences of these two women who both married into the Royal Family — cultural subtext and the rise of social media."]},{"k":"p","s":["Coverage of Meghan has frequently employed coded tropes that target ",["her identity","https://doi.org/10.1080/14680777.2021.1928258"]," as a ",["biracial","https://pressgazette.co.uk/publishers/survey-funds-media-coverage-of-meghan-markle-racist/"],", divorced American woman. This coverage is also amplified by social media algorithms."]},{"k":"p","s":["The comment sections that accompany online stories help create an echo chamber of hostility, highly receptive to the ongoing narrative of the callous daughter and her long-suffering father."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Doreen Lawrence and Prince Harry’s lawsuit against Daily Mail publisher underlines need for Leveson Inquiry part two","https://theconversation.com/doreen-lawrence-and-prince-harrys-lawsuit-against-daily-mail-publisher-underlines-need-for-leveson-inquiry-part-two-192753"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The Thomas Markle revelations matter, not simply because they potentially change what we know about Meghan’s estrangement from her father. They expose how the British media turned that estrangement into a serialized narrative in which Meghan’s silence was used against her."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whether this case warrants a ",["renewed Leveson inquiry","https://www.theguardian.com/media/2018/mar/01/leveson-2-explained-what-was-it-meant-to-achieve"]," is ultimately a policy question. But it demonstrates why the ",["questions Leveson asked","https://doi.org/10.1177/1464884912443495"]," remain unresolved."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem is not just about the degree to which the media may have demonized Meghan. It’s about how confidently it framed a story when one of its central figures could not tell her side until recently."]}],"chars":6874},"https://theconversation.com/ibu-ibu-hingga-suporter-bola-demo-sumpah-pemuda-menandai-meluasnya-kegelisahan-masyarakat-295872":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"72c4e66b92e58977c0d7efc5a7c03d30f91ad7dc9815a90ec9ce2c846b02513e","read":"https://theconversation.com/ibu-ibu-hingga-suporter-bola-demo-sumpah-pemuda-menandai-meluasnya-kegelisahan-masyarakat-295872","bytes":178440,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Ibu-ibu hingga suporter bola: Demo Sumpah Pemuda menandai meluasnya kegelisahan masyarakat","by":[{"n":"Andi Ibnu Masri Rusli","r":"Economy Editor, The Conversation Indonesia"},{"n":"Dicki Mahardika","r":"Podcast Producer, The Conversation Indonesia"},{"n":"Nurul Fitri Ramadhani","r":"Politics + Society Editor, The Conversation Indonesia"},{"n":"Robby Irfany Maqoma","r":"Managing Editor"}],"pub":"2026-11-05T02:00:41Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Jalanan tak lagi jadi panggung milik mahasiswa. Bersamaan dengan momen Sumpah Pemuda segala elemen sosial luruh menjadi satu ruang perlawanan bersama. Ibu-ibu, selebritas, hingga suporter bola bersama sama turun ke jalan dalam satu ruang yang sama."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gelombang unjuk rasa juga bergulir di berbagai kota–mulai dari Jakarta hingga Yogyakarta. Ini bukan lagi sekadar siklus protes musiman, melainkan jadi alarm atas akumulasi ketidakpuasan publik terhadap pemerintah. Ketika ruang hidup tertekan dari berbagai sisi dan respons kekuasaan dinilai nirempati, lalu sejauh mana negara benar benar mendengar kegelisahan warganya?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Melalui podcast SuarAkademia minggu ini, kami mengajak jajaran redaksi The Conversation Indonesia (TCID): Robby Irfany Maqoma (Managing Editor), Nurul Fitri Ramadhani (Editor Politik & Masyarakat), dan juga Andi Ibnu Masri Rusli (Editor Ekonomi) untuk mendiskusikan isu yang jadi diangkat saat unjuk rasa 28 Oktober 2026 lalu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Menurut Nurul, fenomena yang terjadi saat demonstrasi belakangan ini memperlihatkan pergeseran signifikan yang diidentifikasi sebagai broadening of protest constituency atau meluasnya basis konstituensi perlawanan. Jika sebelumnya panggung jalanan kerap didominasi oleh mahasiswa sebagai kelompok intelektual muda, kini barisan demonstrasi dipadati oleh kelompok masyarakat yang jauh lebih heterogen, kaum buruh, aliansi perempuan dan ibu rumah tangga, suporter sepak bola, publik figur, hingga pekerja kantoran yang sebelumnya apolitis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meskipun tiap kelompok membawa beban sektoral yang spesifik, seperti upah layak bagi pekerja, stabilitas harga sembako bagi ibu rumah tangga, hingga kebebasan berekspresi bagi aktivis, mereka bertemu pada satu irisan keresahan yang sama yaitu ketidakpuasan mendalam terhadap cara negara mengelola kebijakan dan kepentingan publik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nurul juga menambahkan bahwa perlawanan masyarakat sipil saat ini lahir secara organik menyerupai rimpang, yang tumbuh mandiri tanpa bergantung pada sosok sentral. Gerakan desentralistis semacam ini secara historis kerap mencemaskan pemegang kekuasaan karena sulit dipatahkan lewat penangkapan tokoh kunci."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sorotan tajam juga mengarah pada penanganan krisis kebakaran hutan dan lahan menahun yang kembali melanda Sumatera, Kalimantan hingga Papua. Robby menilai penanganan pemerintah saat ini terjebak pada capaian adiministrasif belaka, seperti klaim pengiriman helikopter pemadam ataupun pengerahan puluhan ribu personel, tanpa menghasilkan dampak nyata yang memulihkan kualitas udara warga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Masalah ini makin diperparah oleh komunikasi pejabat publik yang dianggap nirempati serta keengganan menetapkan status bencana nasional maupun menerima bantuan internasional, seolah-olah bencana asap telah dinormalisasi menjadi rutinitas tahunan yang lumrah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di sektor ekonomi, Andi melihat tekanan yang dirasakan masyarakat di akar rumput kian nyata di tengah gejolak global, mulai dari lonjakan harga bahan bakar hingga bayang-bayang pajak digital. Keresahan ekonomi ini bahkan memaksa sebagian besar masyarakat kelas menengah ke bawah melakukan penurunan gaya hidup (downgrade lifestyle)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di sisi lain, prioritas anggaran belanja pemerintah mulai dipertanyakan, alokasi dana jumbo untuk program mercusuar berskala ratusan triliun rupiah dinilai rentan dan belum tentu berkelanjutan, dibandingkan jika dialokasikan untuk insentif industri padat karya yang mampu menciptakan lapangan kerja formal jangka panjang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Simak episode lengkapnya hanya di SuarAkademia—ngobrol seru isu terkini, bareng akademisi."]}],"chars":3503},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/italy":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"3acf534a94b272c7fa4563fd6d1255b1bf7651b86d2d53e684e72dc366c37a37","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/italy","bytes":114380,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Italy travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T15:41:31+00:00","mod":"2026-11-03T11:56:35+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice also covers Vatican City."]},{"k":"h","s":["Demonstrations and national strike"]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent demonstrations across northern Italian cities have led to violent riots and looting. There is an increased presence of police and military personnel in Milan. Further demonstrations may take place in major cities. See ",["Political demonstrations","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/italy/safety-and-security#Politicaldemonstrations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about the risks of travel, to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/italy/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Italy set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Italian Embassy in the UK","https://amblondra.esteri.it/en/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Italy follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Lost or stolen passports"]},{"k":"p","s":["If your passport is lost or stolen, you must ",["renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," or ",["apply for an emergency travel document","https://www.gov.uk/travel-urgently-from-abroad-without-uk-passport"],". You cannot use a police report to leave Italy."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel ",["without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Italy, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Italy","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-italy-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries within the previous 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you cannot return to the UK before your visa-free limit expires, contact the nearest ",["local immigration office (‘questura’)","https://questure.poliziadistato.it/"]," (in Italian)."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Italian border control, you may need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your accommodation, for example, a hotel booking confirmation or proof of address for your own property"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your travel insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay – the amount varies depending on your accommodation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must meet the Italian government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Italian Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://vistoperitalia.esteri.it/home/en"],". You’ll need to ",["apply and then book an appointment","https://visa.vfsglobal.com/gbr/en/ita"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Italy with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Italy","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-italy#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual citizenship"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Italian authorities recommend that dual nationals with Italian citizenship enter and leave Italy on an Italian passport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Italy-Slovenia land border"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are temporary border checks at Italy’s border with Slovenia. Allow extra time for crossing the land border. Be ready to show your passport or residency card if you are asked by the border police."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the police"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hotels and accommodation providers in Italy have a legal duty to register your passport details with the police. When checking into your accommodation wait until hotel staff have registered your passport details. Do not leave your passport for later collection. If the hotelier takes a photocopy of your passport, ensure it is either returned to you or destroyed."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’ve come from another Schengen-area country and you are not staying in a hotel or facility that registers your stay, you must declare your presence (‘dichiarazione di presenza’) to the local immigration authority (‘questura’) within 8 days of arriving. The ‘questura’ will give you a form to complete."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get more information from the ",["Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://www.esteri.it/en/servizi-consolari-e-visti/ingressosoggiornoinitalia/condizioni_ingresso/"]," or ",["Italian police force","https://www.poliziadistato.it/articolo/10618"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with people aged 17 and under"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re aged 17 or under, you cannot check into hotels or holiday accommodation without an accompanying adult."]},{"k":"p","s":["British people aged 17 and under travelling without their parents or guardians do not need any authorisation stamped by the Embassy, even if they are resident in Italy. Only Italian children travelling without parents or guardians need such a document stamped by the local police."]},{"k":"p","s":["See further advice on ",["travelling abroad with people aged 17 and under","https://www.gov.uk/permission-take-child-abroad"],", or ",["travelling to the UK with people aged 17 and under","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/children-travelling-to-the-uk/children-travelling-to-the-uk-accessible"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Italy guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/111/italy#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into and out of Italy","https://www.adm.gov.it/portale/en/carta-doganale-viaggiatore"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Italy"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://food.ec.europa.eu/animals/animal-products-movements/personal-imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special food or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Italy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Italy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Italy cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Events in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Italian authorities have increased security around some Jewish community sites due to events in Israel and Palestine. Stay aware of your surroundings, stay away from demonstrations and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations can happen with little or no warning in cities. Most demonstrations are peaceful but can change with little warning."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid any protests, political gatherings or marches. If you are near a demonstration, follow the instructions of the police and local authorities and leave the area. Do not stop to watch or photograph disorder or police activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check local news and official travel information for updates. Transport services maybe cancelled at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are generally low but there are higher levels of petty crime, particularly bag-snatching and pickpocketing, in city centres and at major tourist attractions."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep sight of your belongings at all times"]},{"k":"li","s":["beware of thieves using distraction techniques"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying all your valuables together in handbags or pockets"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave spare cash and valuables in a safe place such as a hotel safe"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Stolen Passports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware that if your passport is stolen, you cannot use a police report to leave Italy. See our ",["lost or stolen passports guidance","https://draft-origin.integration.publishing.service.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/italy/entry-requirements#Lost-or-stolen-passports"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care on public transport, in crowded areas and in city centres, including main train and metro stations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be particularly careful with your belongings:"]},{"k":"li","s":["on public transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["at airports"]},{"k":"li","s":["at tourist sites and local bars, cafes and restaurants"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Theft from cars"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thefts from parked cars is common across the country. Avoid leaving luggage in your vehicle, even out of sight in the boot, for any length of time."]},{"k":"p","s":["Thieves may use a variety of methods to distract you or encourage you to stop your car, including asking for help or directions or pointing out a fictional fault with your car."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking and alcohol"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take drinks from strangers or leave your drinks unattended. Victims of spiked drinks have been robbed and sometimes assaulted. Alcohol and drugs can reduce your vigilance, making you less in control. If you drink, know your limit. Drinks served in bars in Italy are often stronger than those in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Under Italian law, police can stop you at any time to carry out an identity check or your date of entry into the country. Carry photo ID with you at all times. The police will normally ask for your full passport if you are stopped while driving."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Italy have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport regulations"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you buy a ticket from a kiosk or machine, you must validate it on public transport before you start your journey. Officials patrol public transport and will issue an on-the-spot fine if you do not have a validated ticket. Some buses and trams accept onboard contactless payment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tourist tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many major cities in Italy impose a small tax on tourists. You must usually pay this tax at your hotel as it is unlikely to be included in your holiday booking. The rate of tax varies from city to city and can depend on the star rating of the hotel. Hotels often ask for payment in cash. Make sure you get a receipt. For more information, check with the local tourist information office."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Venice access fee"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Venice, you may need to pay an access fee. See ",["when access fees apply, exemptions and how to make a payment","https://cda.ve.it/en/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some Italian towns and cities have specific laws, and you could be fined for breaking them. For example, there may be laws against:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dropping litter"]},{"k":"li","s":["sitting on monument steps"]},{"k":"li","s":["eating and drinking next to main churches, historic monuments and public buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["defacing historic monuments"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s also an offence to enter or bathe in public fountains in many towns and cities, including Florence and Rome or swim in the canals in Venice. You could face a fine of up to 10,000 euros for urinating in a public place."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the island of Capri, you must not use or bring on to the island any disposable plastic objects such as bags, cutlery, plates, cups, food packaging, trays and straws. If you do, you could be fined up to 500 euros."]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal traders operate on the streets of all major Italian cities. It is illegal to buy items from unlicensed street traders. If you do, you could be stopped by the local police and fined."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to remove sand, shells or pebbles from coastal areas in Italy. You could face a large fine for doing so. It’s also illegal to collect various species of flowers, plants and herbs from mountain and wooded areas. For more information, check with the regional authorities of the area you’re visiting."]},{"k":"h","s":["Winter sports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get advice on weather and avalanche conditions before you travel and familiarise yourself with local skiing laws and regulations."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can contact the ",["Italian State Tourist Board","https://www.italia.it/en/contact-us?"]," for advice on safety and weather conditions before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regulations for the ski season include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["from 1 November 2025, all skiers, snowboarders, sledders, and tobogganers will be required to wear CE-certified helmets at all ski resorts. This law applies regardless of age or activity. Failing to do so risks a fine of up to €200 and ski pass suspension for up to 3 days"]},{"k":"li","s":["third-party liability insurance is a legal requirement and can be purchased locally with a ski pass"]},{"k":"li","s":["you must not eat or drink on ski lifts or boarding areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["you must not climb a slope with snowshoes except in an emergency"]},{"k":"li","s":["you must not ski under the influence of alcohol or drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Off-piste skiing is very dangerous, with the danger of avalanches in some areas. Follow all safety instructions and go with a qualified guide. For more information about the avalanche risk, visit the ",["European Avalanche Warning Service","https://www.avalanches.org/"]," website."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your insurance covers off-piste activity. It is a legal requirement for skiers and snowboarders to carry tracking equipment, a snow probe and a shovel if they go off-piste."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["advice on preparing for winter sports","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/winter-sports-stay-safe-on-the-slopes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming and beaches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Every year, people drown in the sea, lakes and in swimming pools in Italy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming pools"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always supervise children. Keep small children within arms-reach in and around swimming pools, even if they can swim or there is a lifeguard present."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Lakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Test the water temperature before swimming in a lake. Cold water shock can be extremely dangerous and overwhelm even the strongest swimmers. See ",["Met Office","https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.metoffice.gov.uk%2Fblog%2F2025%2Fcold-water-shock-how-to-stay-safe&data=05%7C02%7CHannah.Tinker%40fco.gov.uk%7C8406e3c97b21437b7d4b08ded689a0ac%7Cd3a2d0d37cc84f52bbf985bd43d94279%7C0%7C0%7C639184083786937357%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=x1YObGWgabof2nj3%2FpZxZFbpSdDspklXeY2gFzphmOI%3D&reserved=0"]," tips on staying safe."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Beaches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming in the sea. Always supervise children and keep small children within arms-reach. Some beaches may have strong undercurrents."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hidden rocks or shallow depths can cause serious injury or death. Do not dive into unknown water and do not swim at beaches where a river runs into the sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many beaches have a flag system. Make sure you understand the system and follow any warnings (a red flag means you must not enter the water). Take extra care and get local knowledge if there are no lifeguards, flags or signs."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are walking along unmonitored beaches, be aware that waves can come in further than expected and have strong undertows."]},{"k":"p","s":["See further tips on ",["ABTA’s swim safe pages","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow local advice if jellyfish are present."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and adventure sports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hiking, mountaineering and other adventure sports have specific risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your insurance covers these activities."]},{"k":"p","s":["For sports activities like skiing, potholing and mountaineering, and for sports classed as particularly dangerous, such as off-piste skiing, mountain biking, climbing, paragliding or BASE jumping, your insurance should include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["mountain rescue services"]},{"k":"li","s":["helicopter costs"]},{"k":"li","s":["repatriation to your country of residence or transfer to neighbouring countries for treatment"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check weather forecasts and conditions and make sure you’re properly equipped for the worst-case scenario with items such as a map, compass, GPS and telecommunication equipment. Wear appropriate footwear and clothing for the terrain and season."]},{"k":"p","s":["Risks are greater if you undertake any activity alone. Plan your route beforehand and consider your limitations in distance and difficulty. You may want to hire a guide for expert advice. Always leave copies of your itinerary and insurance with someone."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning on hiking in the Trentino region, ",["read what to do if you see a brown bear","https://www.trentino.com/en/leisure-activities/mountains-and-hiking/useful-information/rules-of-conduct-for-bear-contact/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If an accident happens or if you become lost, call 112 for the emergency services."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Italy, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Italy guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/italy/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Italian Police guide on driving in Italy gives further safety advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Italy. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re living in Italy, or planning to live there, see the ",["driving requirements for residents","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-italy#driving-in-italy"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Disabled drivers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Valid ",["Blue Badges","https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/blue-badge-scheme"]," issued in England, Scotland, Wales or Northern Ireland are recognised in Italy and benefit from the same parking and mobility concessions available to holders of the ",["Italian disability parking permit (CUDE)","https://www.disabilita.governo.it/it/contrassegno-unico-disabili-europeo-cude/"],". This includes access to designated disabled parking spaces and, where permitted by local regulations, access to Limited Traffic Zones (ZTLs)."]},{"k":"p","s":["To use your valid Blue Badge in Italy, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["display it clearly at the front of the vehicle (on the dashboard or windscreen)"]},{"k":"li","s":["comply with any local requirements that may apply"]},{"k":"p","s":["The arrangements apply to holders of a valid UK Blue Badge visiting Italy."]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information, read the ",["Circular","https://www.disabilita.governo.it/media/ntijwphx/m_infregistro-ufficialei002362028-09-2026.pdf"]," setting out recognition arrangements and see the GOV.UK guidance on ",["using a Blue Badge in Europe.","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only use officially licensed taxis, which have a taxi sign on the roof and a company name and number written on the side. Call a taxi, order one from an app or pick one up from an official rank."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Transport strikes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Transport strikes are often called at short notice. You can find information on the Ministry of Transport website (in Italian)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pedestrian safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Traffic can be busy, fast and chaotic, especially in the larger cities. Take care when crossing roads. Pedestrians should cross roads at a crossing. You can be fined for crossing the road if you are within 100 metres of a pedestrian crossing but do not use it. Drivers do not always stop, even though they are required to. The green pedestrian crossing signal also allows cars to turn right on to the crossing, so cross with caution."]},{"k":"p","s":["Exercise caution in poorly lit or unfamiliar areas, including in road underpasses."]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency exits in vehicle tunnels are for emergency use only if you need to leave your vehicle and should not be used as pedestrian routes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Traffic restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need a pass to drive into the historic centre of many Italian cities in a private or hire car. You can buy a pass from most car hire companies. The boundaries are usually marked with the letters ZTL in black on a yellow background. If you pass this sign, your registration number is likely to be caught on camera and you will be fined if you do not have a pass."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a ",["congestion charge for Milan city centre","https://www.comune.milano.it/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Rome, city authorities sometimes restrict traffic to reduce pollution. This means certain vehicles are not allowed on the roads in the green band (‘fascia verde’) area, which covers most of Rome. The ",["Rome Municipality","https://romamobilita.it/en"]," has more information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],". For severe weather warnings, visit the ",["European Meteorological Services","https://www.meteoalarm.org/en/?s=italy"]," website."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are a risk during the extended summer months. They are highly dangerous and unpredictable. Check the latest alerts and weather forecast and follow advice of local authorities if you’re considering travelling to affected areas. Take care when visiting or driving through woodland areas and report fires to the emergency services."]},{"k":"p","s":["For information on what to do in the event of a wildfire, visit the ",["Civil Protection Department","https://rischi.protezionecivile.gov.it/en/sezione-con-anticipazioni/forest-fire-risk/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rainfall is common throughout Italy in winter, which can cause local flooding. Monitor local media, weather reports and follow the advice of local authorities in affected areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["High waters are a common occurrence in Venice and can cause flooding in parts of the city."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many parts of Italy lie on a major seismic fault line, which means that minor tremors and earthquakes happen regularly. Learn more about ",["what to do before, during, and after an earthquake","https://rischi.protezionecivile.gov.it/en/seismic-0"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanoes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are ",["several active volcanoes in southern Italy","https://rischi.protezionecivile.gov.it/en/volcanic/volcanoes-italy/"],". National emergency planning is in place for ",["the Phlegraean fields","https://rischi.protezionecivile.gov.it/en/volcanic/volcanoes-italy/phlegraen-fields/bradyseism-phlegraean-fields/"],", an area that remains active experiencing regular tremors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airspace can be affected during eruptions. If you are travelling to or from Catania, during a period of heightened activity, check with your travel provider or with ",["Catania airport","https://www.aeroporto.catania.it/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["what to do in the event of a volcanic eruption","https://rischi.protezionecivile.gov.it/en/volcanic/are-you-prepared/"]," and follow the instructions of the local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 118 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Italy","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/111/italy#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Italy","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/111/italy#General_Information"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["biting insects and ticks"]},{"k":"li","s":["west nile disease"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Italy, including the Alps and the Dolomites. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Italy"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Italy","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/italy-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Italy, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Italy","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-italy"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For advice on what to do when travelling to Italy with medicines containing internationally controlled drugs, see information on the ",["Ministry of Health","https://www.salute.gov.it/new/en/tema/medicinali-stupefacenti-e-precursori-di-droghe/travelling-internationally-medicines-containing/"]," website."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pharmacies"]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need to go to a pharmacy to get most over-the-counter medicines. Pharmacies are widely available and are usually identified by a green cross. UK prescriptions are not accepted, though you may be able to buy an equivalent medication from the pharmacy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alternatively, you can visit an Italian GP to obtain a local prescription. Prescription medicines are not free in Italy, but with an EHIC or GHIC, and an Italian prescription, you will pay a reduced rate."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/mental-health-and-wellbeing-abroad"],". There is also ",["guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Italy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 118"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 115"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 112"]},{"k":"hs","s":["European emergency app"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also download the ",["112 Where Are U app","https://where.areu.lombardia.it/"],", the official European emergency number app. It is only available in some parts of Italy."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?serviceType=lawyers&country=Italy"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Italy"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Italy"]," in Italy"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Italy","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-for-italy"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Italy","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/italy-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/italy/british-embassy-rome"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/italy/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Italy","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-italy"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":28031,"change":"Removal of information about national strike."},"https://theconversation.com/robert-pattinson-is-james-bond-an-unexpected-choice-that-bodes-well-for-the-next-era-of-007-296780":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"70c9e0fcdbea1e35cdc6dc944b08afb0545c43a9c8b833704be12002dc088ad5","read":"https://theconversation.com/robert-pattinson-is-james-bond-an-unexpected-choice-that-bodes-well-for-the-next-era-of-007-296780","bytes":176104,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Robert Pattinson is James Bond – an unexpected choice that bodes well for the next era of 007","by":[{"n":"James Chapman","r":"Professor of Film Studies, University of Leicester"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T17:14:06Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Speculation over the next 007 has been fervent ever since Daniel Craig announced his departure after his fifth outing as the spy in No Time to Die (2021). That search has now ended with 40-year-old British actor Robert Pattinson confirmed as the new James Bond."]},{"k":"p","s":["The intensity of the guessing game is a testament both to the public’s enduring fascination ",["Bond","https://theconversation.com/topics/james-bond-6087"]," and to the expectations that now rest on Pattinson’s shoulders as the longest-running continuous series in cinema history moves into a new era at Amazon Studios."]},{"k":"p","s":["For Amazon, the drawn-out casting process has generated valuable free publicity at a time when there was no real news about Bond 26."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["James Bond is now controlled by Amazon – the franchise’s history holds clues to the future of 007","https://theconversation.com/james-bond-is-now-controlled-by-amazon-the-franchises-history-holds-clues-to-the-future-of-007-250563"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Unlike previous Bond castings, this one has been played out on social media, aided by our 24-hour news cycle, with its insatiable appetite for content. In 2024 several reputable media outlets ran with a story that ",["Aaron Taylor-Johnson","https://theconversation.com/the-ideal-james-bond-is-an-actor-on-the-cusp-of-superstardom-as-film-history-shows-226281"]," was about to be announced as the new Bond. That proved to be a false dawn – albeit rather more plausible than the hoax announcement that Australian model ",["Finlay Light","https://www.mi6-hq.com/sections/articles/bonds-finlay-light-interview"]," had been cast in 1986. Most recently, Josh O'Connor and Callum Turner appeared to be among the strongest contenders."]},{"k":"h","s":["Bond legacies"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pattinson will be only the seventh actor to play Bond on the big screen in 65 years. Inevitably there will be comparisons with his predecessors."]},{"k":"p","s":["For many fans, ",["Sean Connery","https://theconversation.com/sean-connery-bond-james-bond-but-so-much-more-149238"]," remains the original and best, incarnating the suave but ruthless secret agent with a licence to kill in seven pictures from Dr No (1962) to Never Say Never Again (1983)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Connery was the only actor whom Bond’s creator ",["Ian Fleming","https://theconversation.com/topics/ian-fleming-38653"]," met, and contrary to popular belief, the author approved of the casting. He wrote in a ",["letter","https://www.dawn.com/news/1824618"]," that “the man they have chosen for Bond, Sean Connery, is a real charmer – fairly unknown but a good actor with the right looks and physique”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Sean Connery: ‘Bond, James Bond’, but so much more","https://theconversation.com/sean-connery-bond-james-bond-but-so-much-more-149238"]]},{"k":"p","s":["When Connery stepped down for the first time, following You Only Live Twice (1967), Australian model George Lazenby, the only Bond actor who can genuinely be described as “unknown”, was a one-off Bond in On Her Majesty’s Secret Service (1969). But it was ",["Roger Moore","https://theconversation.com/topics/roger-moore-38988"],", at the time one of the biggest television stars in the world (after roles in The Saint and The Persuaders!), who made a lighter but popular replacement in seven continuous films, from Live and Let Die (1973) to A View to a Kill (1985)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Arguably the best actor to play Bond, the classically trained Timothy Dalton, was a late replacement for Pierce Brosnan, tied to a contract for a cancelled television show in 1986."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalton’s performance remains the closest psychologically to Fleming’s character, although his tenure lasted only two films. The announcement of Brosnan’s casting for GoldenEye (1995) came as no surprise and in the decade since he “lost” the role, he had matured into it. Brosnan successfully restored the popular appeal of the Bond series in four films until Die Another Day (2002)."]},{"k":"p","s":["And then came Craig, a controversial choice for being “too short” and “too blonde”, who proved the naysayers wrong in five box-office blockbusters from Casino Royale (2006) to No Time to Die (2021)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Bond futures"]},{"k":"p","s":["In certain respects, the casting of Pattinson seems a left-field choice, just as Craig’s was. His name was a late addition to the shortlist of candidates leaked (or, possibly, trailed to gauge public opinion) over recent weeks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pattinson also differs from all the other Bonds in having box-office pedigree from mainstream movie franchises, including Edward Cullen in the ",["Twilight","https://theconversation.com/topics/twilight-3466"]," saga and Batman in The Batman (2022). If this suggests safety-first casting for Amazon, we should bear in mind that Pattinson has also done his share of edgy, independent films with directors including David Cronenberg and Werner Herzog."]},{"k":"p","s":["I expect there’ll be some kickback online, as there was with Craig. Bond fans can be extremely territorial about “their” hero. But Pattinson has a lot going for him. He’s the right sort of age: James Bond is an experienced agent who requires some maturity and gravitas. He’s tall and good looking in a slightly odd sort of way, perhaps suggesting something of the ",["“alien and un-English”","https://books.google.co.uk/books/about/Moonraker.html?id=33LWoQEACAAJ&redir_esc=y"]," quality that Fleming identified in his hero. And Pattinson showed that he had something “Bondian” about him in Christopher Nolan’s Tenet (2020)."]},{"k":"p","s":["An important point I take away from this news, given the widely-aired concern that Amazon don’t properly understand the Bond franchise, is that Pattinson’s casting indicates the studio is going to maintain Bond’s essential Britishness."]},{"k":"p","s":["With Denis Villeneuve in the director’s chair and Peaky Blinders’ Stephen Knight writing the script, the next Bond picture will be another reset for the series. I think Amazon have made a good call. This will be a new dawn, not twilight, for James Bond."]}],"chars":4898},"https://theconversation.com/du-pain-et-des-jeux-a-washington-d-c-ou-limaginaire-imperial-de-donald-trump-294585":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"2a13e5cde1277d66ff5bcccdfd1f6396d7fec901487028b4a1bf84e772571412","read":"https://theconversation.com/du-pain-et-des-jeux-a-washington-d-c-ou-limaginaire-imperial-de-donald-trump-294585","bytes":184374,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Du pain et des jeux à Washington D.C., ou l’imaginaire impérial de Donald Trump","by":[{"n":"Robert Chaouad","r":"Adjunct assistant professor, City University of New York"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T16:14:13Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["L’ESSENTIEL"]},{"k":"li","s":["Les 250 ans de l’indépendance américaine devaient célébrer l’unité d’une nation profondément divisée."]},{"k":"li","s":["Donald Trump a détourné les commémorations pour mettre en scène sa propre gloire et son pouvoir."]},{"k":"li","s":["Comme à l’époque de la Rome antique, le divertissement devient un instrument politique pour masquer les difficultés du pays."]},{"k":"p","s":["La célébration du 250e anniversaire de la Déclaration d’indépendance américaine, officiellement en ",["préparation depuis 2016","https://america250.org/"],", aura tourné à l’exercice de promotion des volontés présidentielles et aura contribué à alimenter les divisions du pays. Loin de célébrer la République américaine née le 4 juillet 1776 et en quête d’une « Union plus parfaite » (selon les mots de la Constitution américaine), cette séquence trumpienne aura été nourrie aux sources d’un autre imaginaire politique. En effet, des pratiques de pouvoir développées sous la Rome impériale semblent trouver un écho auprès du président des États-Unis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dans un entretien accordé au ",["New York Times, le 15 juin 2026","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/03/opinion/mary-beard-trump-ancient-rome.html"],", l’historienne et helléniste Mary Beard, professeure à l’université de Cambridge (Royaume-Uni) et spécialiste de la Rome antique, expliquait que la référence à la Rome ancienne semblait, sur certains aspects, flagrante, même s’il importait d’éviter les comparaisons personnelles directes. Elle relevait ainsi comment la volonté du président Trump de faire construire à Washington D. C. le plus grand arc de triomphe du monde, sa manière de changer d’avis sur certains sujets ou encore sa volonté d’apparaître sur les pièces ou billets de monnaie résonnaient avec des pratiques observaient sous la Rome ancienne."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Des dollars à l’effigie de Trump ? Une pratique rarissime hors des monarchies","https://theconversation.com/des-dollars-a-leffigie-de-trump-une-pratique-rarissime-hors-des-monarchies-292246"]]},{"k":"p","s":["En juillet 2026, deux journalistes du New York Times, Maggie Haberman et Jonathan Swan, publiaient un livre-enquête, ",["Regime Change. Inside the Imperial Presidency of Donald Trump","https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Regime-Change/Maggie-Haberman/9781668067246"],", consacré à ce que la pratique débridée du pouvoir de Donald Trump, depuis son retour à la présidence, faisait subir au système politique américain. Empruntant l’expression d’imperial presidency (présidence impériale) à l’historien Arthur Schlesinger, ",["qui l’avait forgée en 1973","https://shs.cairn.info/la-presidence-imperiale--9782738120281-page-57"],", à l’époque du scandale du Watergate, pour décrire le renforcement des pouvoirs présidentiels au cours de l’histoire américaine, les journalistes ont appliqué cette référence à la seconde présidence Trump."]},{"k":"p","s":["Leur conclusion semble sans appel : la Constitution américaine fait face à des attaques sans précédent. Les contre-pouvoirs institutionnels vacillent (la Cour suprême a entériné de nombreuses actions litigieuses du président), lorsqu’ils n’abdiquent pas directement leur pouvoir (le Congrès a renoncé à exercer certaines de ses prérogatives constitutionnelles au profit du président, même dans le registre budgétaire) ; le président teste les limites de la Constitution en adoptant des décrets (executive orders) à tout-va, même dans des domaines qu’elle ne lui reconnaît pas ; il tente de s’arroger des pouvoirs que la Constitution ne lui confère pas, envoie la Garde nationale dans les villes et abuse du ",["recours à l’état d’urgence","https://www.cato.org/commentary/trumps-emergencies-are-pretexts-undermining-constitution"]," (emergency powers), pour gouverner sans le consentement du Congrès."]},{"k":"h","s":["« Panem et circenses »"]},{"k":"p","s":["Par-delà la dimension strictement institutionnelle de l’exercice du pouvoir, il est une autre pratique du pouvoir caractéristique de la Rome impériale qui résonne aujourd’hui avec l’exercice trumpien du pouvoir : l’usage du divertissement comme instrument politique."]},{"k":"p","s":["Panem et circenses, « du pain et des jeux du cirque », cette expression forgée par le poète et satiriste romain Juvénal autour de l’an 100 avant notre ère, apparaît dans sa Satire X, au vers 81. Le satiriste y dénonçait l’apathie du peuple romain, prêt à se laisser corrompre à grands coups de spectacles et de divertissements organisés par les autorités municipales et impériales."]},{"k":"p","s":["La formule aura également servi de trame et de titre à l’une des œuvres majeures de l’historien Paul Veyne, qui avait publié, en 1976, ",["Le pain et le cirque : sociologie historique d’un pluralisme politique","https://www.seuil.com/ouvrage/le-pain-et-le-cirque-sociologie-historique-d-un-pluralisme-politique-paul-veyne/9782020045070"],". Ne se contentant pas de dénoncer une stratégie de distraction en vue du contrôle des masses, l’historien montrait comment la pratique qui consistait à offrir au peuple romain des libéralités sous la forme de spectacles et de blé s’apparentait autant à une obligation qu’à une démonstration de pouvoir et de prestige, de la part des notables romains et de l’empereur lui-même."]},{"k":"p","s":["Offrir du cirque, plus que du pain d’ailleurs ; divertir pour divertir l’attention, c’est ce qui semble avoir inspiré le président Trump quand il s’est agi de célébrer les 250 ans de la Déclaration d’indépendance. En effet, on ne peut s’empêcher de penser à cette référence de la Rome ancienne lorsque l’on se penche sur les tours qu’a pris cette année d’anniversaire : non seulement la forme des célébrations, mais aussi la posture politique de celui qui les a promus et le contexte dans lequel les commémorations se sont déroulées."]},{"k":"h","s":["Combat de MMA à la Maison-Blanche"]},{"k":"p","s":["Combat de MMA (Mixed Martial Arts) dans les jardins de la Maison-Blanche, seize jours de ",["Foire à Washington D.C","https://freedom250.org/celebration/the-great-american-state-fair"],". réunissant les États et territoires des États-Unis, ",["jeux patriotiques pour la jeunesse","https://freedom250.org/celebration/the-2026-patriot-games"]," américaine, ",["pièces frappées à l’effigie du président","https://www.usmint.gov/campaigns/donald-trump-coin?srsltid=AU7gw4VGGa_4yAZjXfrbci-Vl_HBSviQEPjHc-4rZ2l5Zt-4xytT8-dy"],", feux d’artifice géants, course de voitures dans les rues de la capitale, etc. Plutôt que de s’en remettre à ",["America 250","https://america250.org/"]," (la commission bipartisane créée par le Congrès, en 2016, pour organiser les célébrations), l’administration Trump a préféré développer sa propre initiative, ",["Freedom 250","https://www.freedom250.org/"],", financée par des acteurs privés et par les fonds initialement alloués à la commission America 250. Cette initiative aura permis à l’administration de reprendre le contrôle de l’événement et de le redessiner à son image."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tel l’empereur romain assistant à ces jeux et souhaitant être vu, quand il ne descendait pas lui-même dans l’arène, ces jeux et divertissements ont donné lieu à une mise en scène de l’exercice du pouvoir où tous les regards convergeaient vers un seul. Toutefois, au lieu de mettre en avant l’unité du pays, ces célébrations n’auront fait que révéler son intense polarisation politique. En effet, loin d’attirer les foules sur une base transpartisane, ces divertissements auront donné aux supporters du président une occasion de célébrer leur héros, tandis que ses opposants n’auront que peu goûté ces distractions, délaissant ces initiatives pour ne pas cautionner les dérives autoritaires de l’administration Trump."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le contexte dans lequel ces commémorations ont pris place laissait également à penser que ces initiatives avaient pour objectif de détourner l’attention du peuple américain, ou à tout le moins d’une partie de celui-ci. À quelques semaines des élections de mi-mandat, ces jeux du cirque pouvaient ainsi s’interpréter comme un moyen de dissimuler les échecs du président, à commencer par l’incapacité de l’économie américaine à offrir du pain à sa population, en particulier aux classes sociales populaires qui soutenaient Trump jusque-là."]},{"k":"p","s":["Car c’est là l’une des réalités les plus criantes des politiques menées par l’administration Trump : renforcer, sans vergogne et au su de tous, la logique d’une économie à deux vitesses, où une large majorité des classes moyennes et populaires se démène dans un quotidien incertain, fait de hausse du prix des matières premières, de l’inflation, des taux d’intérêt, du coût de la vie quotidienne, et cela en raison des décisions prises par le président (imposition de droits de douane, ",["baisse des impôts pour les classes aisées et les entreprises","https://www.americanprogress.org/article/7-ways-the-big-beautiful-bill-cuts-taxes-for-the-rich/"],", guerre en Iran), tandis qu’une frange infime de la population profite du dynamisme de l’économie."]},{"k":"p","s":["Portés par les valeurs de l’intelligence artificielle, les marchés s’envolent, au risque de former une nouvelle bulle financière ; dans le même temps, la famille Trump s’enrichit tous azimuts – profitant de la ",["confusion entre intérêts privés et publics","https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2026/09/21/jared-kushners-dollar-diplomacy"]," –, tout comme un groupe restreint d’acteurs économiques qui aura su s’acheter un accès privilégié au chef de l’État et à toutes les politiques publiques et ",["décisions adoptées par son administration","https://www.wsj.com/business/media/david-ellison-renames-combined-paramount-warner-as-skydance-203c081b"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Corrompre pour divertir"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cette contradiction, qui échappe de moins en moins à l’attention du pays, aura conduit le président à tenter de rectifier, à quelques semaines des élections de mi-mandat, le désarroi suscité par sa politique économique. Puisque ses recettes économiques n’ont pas réussi à fournir du pain à la population américaine, il s’est senti l’obligation, lors de la convention du parti républicain, le 9 septembre 2026, de promettre la ",["distribution d’un chèque de 5 000 dollars","https://www.wsj.com/opinion/donald-trump-5000-dividend-midterm-elections-f2643cf3"]," à tout citoyen adulte si le parti républicain conservait la majorité au Congrès."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Trump peut-il acheter les midterms ?","https://theconversation.com/trump-peut-il-acheter-les-midterms-293621"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Cette proposition, qui a surpris et effaré jusque dans le camp des proches conseillers du président, ",["aurait coûté 1 000 milliards de dollars","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/10/us/politics/trump-dividend-5000-check.html"]," à un pays qui accuse déjà une dette publique de 40 000 milliards de dollars, et sans que l’on sache comment une telle mesure pourrait être financée. Certains auront associé cette démarche à une ",["tentative de corruption pour achat de votes à quelques semaines des élections","https://theconversation.com/how-anti-bribery-laws-apply-to-trumps-promise-of-5-000-payments-if-republicans-keep-control-of-congress-291722"],", quand d’autres y auront vu des résonances avec les conditions qui avaient conduit à la chute de l’empire romain. Corruption et divertissement, deux pratiques associées aux usages du pain et du cirque en politique qui avaient participé à la ruine des finances publiques de cet empire sur fond d’appauvrissement de la population, de non-paiement de leurs impôts par les élites et d’inflation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les célébrations du 250e anniversaire de l’Indépendance auront certes satisfait les tenants du mouvement MAGA et l’hôte de la Maison-Blanche, qui aura ainsi pu assouvir son imaginaire politique de grand homme et de leader tout-puissant, mais elles auront aussi précipité le pays dans une fuite en avant aux allures de fin de règne impérial – régime dont la Déclaration d’indépendance américaine de 1776 entendait se défaire et que les Pères fondateurs de la Constitution américaine, en 1787, entendaient éviter."]}],"chars":10035},"https://theconversation.com/why-using-a-chatbot-as-your-lawyer-is-a-risky-move-and-ties-up-our-court-system-296255":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-19T04:32Z","sha":"d35d38724963ddc7104ee98ec88dc80e54f7ee5f0889bc66ef8abfb5a380ab64","read":"https://theconversation.com/why-using-a-chatbot-as-your-lawyer-is-a-risky-move-and-ties-up-our-court-system-296255","bytes":181925,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Why using a chatbot as your lawyer is a risky move – and ties up our court system","by":[{"n":"Felicity Bell","r":"Deputy Director, Centre for the Future of the Legal Profession, UNSW"},{"n":"Michael Legg","r":"Professor of Law, UNSW"},{"n":"Vicki McNamara","r":"Senior Research Associate, Centre for the Future of the Legal Profession, UNSW"}],"pub":"2026-11-19T03:21:10Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In the Federal Court of Australia, applications by self-represented litigants, many using artificial intelligence (AI) to research and draft their claims, ",["have skyrocketed","https://www.afr.com/work-and-careers/workplace/courts-on-alert-as-ai-brings-a-torrent-of-sloppy-workplace-claims-20260730-p60jw5"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Fair Work Commission, a federal tribunal, has already seen ",["a jump in filings","https://www.fwc.gov.au/about-us/news-and-media/news/ai-and-increased-workload-commission"],", many of them “AI slop”."]},{"k":"p","s":["These experiences are also reflected in our centre’s global database of AI-related cases. It contains 295 Australian cases (to September 30 2026) in which a court or tribunal identified problematic use of AI in legal proceedings. Examples include citing made-up case law, citing law that is real but irrelevant to the case, and using AI to write witness statements or submissions that aren’t entirely accurate."]},{"k":"p","s":["The database shows a huge increase in cases where these types of AI misuse has been mentioned over the past year, with self-represented litigants accounting for 81% of Australian misuse cases."]},{"k":"h","s":["Chatbots can make poor lawyers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Access to courts is a fundamental part of access to justice. But starting court proceedings without a viable or valid claim wastes time, causes stress and may have severe financial consequences for the person bringing the case."]},{"k":"p","s":["People might use chatbots built on large language models to help them with a legal matter in different ways:"]},{"k":"li","s":["advice about the law generally but also how it specifically applies to their own situation"]},{"k":"li","s":["drafting of court documents to commence or defend a case"]},{"k":"li","s":["drafting of court documents to support the case, such as submissions (legal arguments for why the person should succeed or their opponent not succeed) or statements about the facts (such as affidavits or witness statements)."]},{"k":"p","s":["While AI might ",["usefully assist people","https://doi.org/10.1111/spol.70131"]," to do all of these things, generative AI chatbots are ",["much more sycophantic than humans","https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.aec8352"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lawyers have a duty to always act in their clients’ best interests, which sometimes means challenging clients’ views and delivering unpopular opinions. AI chatbots have no such obligations."]},{"k":"p","s":["There may also be errors in the material that they generate. For example, in ",["Sadnan Khan v Aldi Pty Ltd","https://www.austlii.edu.au/cgi-bin/viewdoc/au/cases/cth/FWC/2026/3144.html"],", the Fair Work Commission took the unusual step of ordering costs of A$1,230 against a former Aldi employee who tried to sue for unfair dismissal. The commission found Khan had relied on AI-generated arguments even though he should have realised his claim was doomed to fail. (Leave to appeal was ",["refused","https://www.austlii.edu.au/cgi-bin/viewdoc/au/cases/cth/FWCFB/2026/268.html"],")."]},{"k":"p","s":["To use AI successfully, people need to be able to check sources, verify information and ultimately explain the relevance of the legal arguments they are trying to make."]},{"k":"h","s":["The higher the court, the riskier AI-use becomes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The main impact of poor use of AI is twofold. First, most people are not successful, either because their legal argument doesn’t work, or the facts (as found by the court or tribunal) don’t support the argument, or both."]},{"k":"p","s":["Two unpublished papers using data from US courts in civil matters show a similar pattern: large increases in court filings ",["by self-represented people using AI","https://ssrn.com/abstract=6766859"]," but no apparent change to win rates, which ",["remain low","https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.29493"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, the recent Australian Federal Court data show unsuccessful claims are now working their way up the court food chain. A high proportion of the increase in filings is made up of appeals from people who were unsuccessful in lower courts or tribunals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Litigating in higher courts, such as the Federal Court, is riskier. The ",["“loser pays” rule of legal costs often applies","https://www.auspublaw.org/blog/2024/6/bruce-lehrmann-went-back-for-his-hat-and-lost-his-shirt-costs-in-australian-litigation"]," (though not for some types of case). This is different from lower-tier courts and tribunals, which are often “no cost” jurisdictions, meaning costs are not routinely ordered."]},{"k":"p","s":["Besides ordering costs, what have courts and tribunals been doing about this increasing workload?"]},{"k":"p","s":["As we explain in a ",["recent article","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/cambridge-forum-on-ai-law-and-governance/article/putting-the-genai-back-into-the-bottle-judicial-regulation-of-generative-artificial-intelligence-in-legal-proceedings/CE4225FA88EB4FE6EADD8D3D82C7A06A"],", Australian courts are not alone – similar issues are being faced in many countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Broadly, courts have adopted a pyramid of responses, beginning with education at the base. Most Australian courts have now released ",["guidance about the responsible use of generative AI in legal proceedings","https://www.unsw.edu.au/content/dam/images/law/centre-for-the-future-of-the-legal-profession/research/2025-03-research_docs/2026-03-CFLP%20-%20GenAI%20use%20in%20litigation%20-%20Australian%20courts%20and%20legal%20regulator%20guidance%20(March%202026)%203.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Fair Work Commission’s guidance, effective from October 20 2026, explains the importance of real legal sources, and even suggests how to prompt AI chatbots more effectively."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Singapore, courts are exploring ",["their own AI-powered tools for users in small claims matters","https://www.judiciary.gov.sg/news-and-resources/news/news-details/media-release--new-generative-ai-powered-case-summarisation-tool-to-help-small-claims-tribunals-users"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The next layer involves corrective measures, such as permitting a person to amend and refile documents, and giving warnings about future sanctions. Where stronger actions are warranted, courts and tribunals are responding with a range of deterrent options: striking out all or part of a claim or defence; imposing restrictions on filing of further materials; and of course the significant costs that can be incurred. At the very apex of the pyramid is the possibility of legal or even criminal sanction via the laws of contempt of court."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, warnings and sanctions alone are unlikely to solve the problem of self-represented litigants misusing AI. The difficulty? ",["People like the responses produced by generative AI","https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.aec8352"],". It feels supportive and encouraging, and can produce fluent-sounding arguments far quicker than a human could draft them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Where access to legal advice can be costly and hard to obtain, AI chatbots are always available and often free. AI is already becoming part of how people engage with the justice system. The real challenge for courts is ensuring people have the knowledge and support needed to use AI responsibly to improve their case, instead of sabotaging it."]}],"chars":5414},"https://theconversation.com/fossil-of-the-day-has-mark-carney-made-canada-a-climate-heretic-296908":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-22T13:52Z","sha":"afc833e37b7d29ba89fb09ae2aced842c2e87fb22116e27281fa725ae277db1c","read":"https://theconversation.com/fossil-of-the-day-has-mark-carney-made-canada-a-climate-heretic-296908","bytes":182352,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Fossil of the Day: Has Mark Carney made Canada a climate heretic?","by":[{"n":"David Tindall","r":"Professor of Sociology, University of British Columbia"},{"n":"Mark CJ Stoddart","r":"Professor, Department of Sociology, Memorial University of Newfoundland"}],"pub":"2026-11-22T12:44:37Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Climate activists at ",["COP31 in Antalya, Turkey","https://theconversation.com/topics/cop31-129714"],", awarded Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney a ",["Fossil of the Day award","https://www.theglobeandmail.com/canada/article-carney-awarded-satirical-fossil-of-the-day-title-by-activists-over/"],", along with other leaders from wealthy countries who skipped the summit."]},{"k":"p","s":["The satirical award is given to countries and leaders seen as doing little to support efforts to tackle climate change."]},{"k":"p","s":["The award was not the only criticism of Carney’s climate credentials. ",["Newsweek","https://www.newsweek.com/revenge-of-climate-heretics-50-leading-eco-policy-dissenters-12651706"]," listed the prime minister at No. 2 on a list of “climate heretics,” just behind Microsoft founder Bill Gates and ahead of United States President Donald Trump."]},{"k":"p","s":["These criticisms might seem surprising, as Carney has been seen as a climate champion. ",["At the 2015 COP in Paris","https://bsky.app/profile/dbtindall.bsky.social/post/3lkgsfwerk22e"],", Carney said companies need to ",["develop plans for net-zero emissions","https://youtu.be/JAqfg8JwASg?si=IzAvPFvjFfE81HJH"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, after becoming prime minister, he scrapped the federal consumer carbon tax and signed an agreement with Alberta to push forward a new oil pipeline. How should we make sense of the Fossil of the Day award? How did Carney go from seeming climate hero to climate villain?"]},{"k":"p","s":["As sociologists, ",["we have written about","https://doi.org/10.1080/08941920.2023.2175284"]," and ",["researched environmental activism","https://doi.org/10.1080/17524032.2024.2377719"]," around COP summits. These gatherings are not only places for policy discussions. They provide a platform for activists to push for action and direct criticism toward obstructive governments and corporations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Fossil of the Day as a strategic event"]},{"k":"p","s":["Social movements take advantage of global events such as COP to ",["name and shame political leaders or corporations that they identify as climate villains","https://arpbooks.org/product/a-world-to-win/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["At COP summits, the ",["Climate Action Network","https://climatenetwork.org/"]," hosts the Fossil of the Day award, as well as some other awards. The ceremony resembles a TV comedy sketch, where activists describe the key climate negotiation events they wish to highlight, and set out to embarrass those obstructing progress."]},{"k":"p","s":["While this is going on, a person in a dinosaur suit dances and music from Jurassic Park plays. Meanwhile, activists sing songs with lyrics they make up for the event."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fossil of the Day is about taking advantage of a critical event. Groups like the Climate Action Network award ",["Fossils of the Day","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0LerHay2eBM"]," to try to affect media coverage, ",["influence public opinion","https://vancouversun.com/opinion/op-ed/opinion-the-climate-conundrum-facing-political-leaders-the-public-wants-to-have-it-both-ways"]," and ultimately pressure governments to take greater action to tackle climate change."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some critical events like COP happen on a regular schedule that is known in advance. We have referred to these as ",["regularly scheduled critical events","https://doi.org/10.1080/08941920.2023.2175284"],". Groups can plan ahead and take advantage of opportunities to comment on and critique the conversations going on in official spaces of deliberation among global leaders."]},{"k":"p","s":["Relatedly, ",["interaction ritual theory explains phenomena that often occur in the context of a common action or event","https://doi.org/10.1007/s11186-024-09587-y"],". Some key elements of the process include: group assembly (bodily co-presence), mutual focus of attention and shared mood."]},{"k":"p","s":["Engagement in interaction rituals often fosters group solidarity, emotional energy, symbols of social relationship and standards of morality. We can think about the Fossil of the Day in these terms."]},{"k":"p","s":["Activists and other COP participants routinely try to attend the Fossil of the Day award. It is an opportunity to meet up and rub elbows. Participants benefit from camaraderie, some light-hearted humour, and also, in some cases, righteous anger directed at leaders, governments and other bodies who obstruct climate action. These get-togethers reinforce social ties among the participants."]},{"k":"h","s":["Canada: Climate hero to climate villain?"]},{"k":"p","s":["At COP21 in Paris, then-Prime Minister Justin Trudeau announced, ",["“Canada is back!”","https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-video-watch-the-highlights-of-justin-trudeaus-cop21-speech-in-under/"]," The Trudeau government’s environment minister, Catherine McKenna, helped to negotiate the ",["Paris Climate Agreement","https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/mckenna-cop21-paris-goal-1.3355409"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["One of Carney’s first acts as prime minister was to cancel the consumer carbon tax Trudeau brought in. And, among other things, ",["Carney is now working to develop new oil and gas projects","https://theconversation.com/mark-carney-wants-to-make-canada-an-energy-superpower-but-what-will-be-sacrificed-for-that-goal-255079"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["At COP31, Carney was a no-show at the leaders summit. This past week, two former environment and climate change ministers criticized the record and direction of the current government. McKenna stated that the claim that Canada is still committed to its targets is ",["“factually untrue.”","https://globalnews.ca/news/12151036/canada-paris-targets/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Indeed, ",["Canada consistently has one of the worst climate performance records","https://fernwoodpublishing.ca/books/thirty-years-of-failure"],". The Climate Change Performance Index, which compares the climate performance of 64 countries and the European Union, ",["ranks Canada 62nd","https://ccpi.org/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This poor performance started ",["before Carney’s tenure as prime minister","https://doi.org/10.1080/08941920.2020.1783730"],", but Canada has been backsliding on the climate change file since he took office."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the view of many Canadians, Canada faces serious, and even existential, threats from the Trump-led United States. In the wake of this threat, Carney has been trying to boost economic growth and diversify international and domestic trade."]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of this has involved plans to ",["grow the fossil fuel sector","https://macdonaldlaurier.ca/carney-wants-canada-to-become-an-energy-superpower-where-will-the-money-come-from-david-detomasi-in-the-hub/"],". The strategy has also been an attempt to ",["assuage discontent fuelling separatist sentiments","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/20/world/canada/carney-alberta-referendum-trump.html"]," in oil-rich Alberta."]},{"k":"p","s":["What is not entirely clear is whether the direction of Carney’s energy and climate policies is a short-term strategy to deal with these crises, or a longer-term pivot away from climate action."]}],"chars":5019},"https://theconversation.com/nsw-has-passed-a-special-law-for-one-coal-mine-heres-why-thats-worrying-296703":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T05:31Z","sha":"f621a7fda1f42a833bb952b2e258af765864ed426cec5eb8461452cfcc6f8f20","read":"https://theconversation.com/nsw-has-passed-a-special-law-for-one-coal-mine-heres-why-thats-worrying-296703","bytes":184278,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"NSW has passed a special law for one coal mine. Here’s why that’s worrying","by":[{"n":"Katherine Owens","r":"Associate Professor of Environmental Law, University of Sydney"}],"pub":"2026-11-23T04:23:33Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["A new law sets a concerning precedent for climate action in one Australian state."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the early hours of November 21, the New South Wales parliament passed a ",["special law","https://www.parliament.nsw.gov.au/parliamentary-business/bills/bill-details?billId=18979&ref=3287"]," that applies to a single coal mine, the Mount Pleasant open-cut ",["coal mine","https://machenergyaustralia.com.au/mount-pleasant/"]," in NSW’s Upper Hunter region. The ",["Mount Pleasant Mine Act","https://files.parliament.nsw.gov.au/fileapi/ParlFiles/GetArtifact/Second%20Print.pdf?serverRelativeUrl=%2Fbill%2Ffiles%2F18979%2FSecond%20Print.pdf"]," will allow the mine to dig up to 16.5 million tonnes of coal a year until the end of 2032."]},{"k":"p","s":["This new law is worrying for several reasons."]},{"k":"p","s":["The law comes just weeks after a landmark ",["High Court ruling","https://theconversation.com/australias-top-court-puts-fossil-fuel-developers-on-notice-293680"]," related to the Mount Pleasant mine, that was celebrated by experts and environmentalists as a win for emissions reduction."]},{"k":"p","s":["The new law works around that decision. It also lets the government change how almost any NSW law applies to the Mount Pleasant mine."]},{"k":"h","s":["How did we get here?"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2022, the NSW Independent Planning Commission approved a major expansion of the Mount Pleasant mine, owned by mining company ",["MACH Energy","https://machenergyaustralia.com.au/mount-pleasant/"],". A local community group ",["challenged","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-07-24/mount-pleasant-coal-mine-expansion-halted-by-court/105566836"]," that approval in court, and on October 7, the High Court ",["ruled","https://www.hcourt.gov.au/sites/default/files/eresources/2026-10-07/HCA/MACH%20Energy%20Australia%20Pty%20Ltd%20v%20Denman%20Aberdeen%20Muswellbrook%20Scone%20Healthy%20Environment%20Group%20Inc%20%28S174-2025%29%20%5B2026%5D%20HCA%2035.pdf"]," in its favour."]},{"k":"p","s":["The majority found the planning commission had not properly considered setting conditions to cut emissions, including ",["scope 3 emissions","https://cer.gov.au/schemes/national-greenhouse-and-energy-reporting-scheme/about-emissions-and-energy-data/emissions-and-energy-types"]," from coal burned overseas, to the “ ",["greatest extent practicable","https://legislation.nsw.gov.au/view/whole/html/inforce/current/epi-2021-0731#sec.2.20"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["The High Court did not set any such conditions or ban the expansion, but ",["sent the case","https://www.hcourt.gov.au/sites/default/files/eresources/2026-10-07/HCA/MACH%20Energy%20Australia%20Pty%20Ltd%20v%20Denman%20Aberdeen%20Muswellbrook%20Scone%20Healthy%20Environment%20Group%20Inc%20%28S174-2025%29%20%5B2026%5D%20HCA%2035.pdf"]," back to the NSW Land and Environment Court. That court was due to hear the case ",["in December","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-10/mount-pleasant-mine-expansion-laws-chris-minns/107369370"],". Until then, the mine could only produce 12.5 million tonnes of coal a year under an older permit."]},{"k":"p","s":["MACH Energy said this put about ",["400 jobs","https://www.nsw.gov.au/ministerial-releases/minns-labor-government-steps-to-protect-400-hunter-jobs-ahead-of-christmas"]," at risk before Christmas. Those jobs are in NSW’s Hunter region, a ",["key battleground","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/nsw-passes-hunter-valley-coalmine-law-as-greens-claim-change-an-attempt-to-head-off-one-nation-ntwnfb"]," for One Nation at the March state election."]},{"k":"p","s":["The state government responded to the court ruling by taking the issue to parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Australia’s top court puts fossil fuel developers on notice","https://theconversation.com/australias-top-court-puts-fossil-fuel-developers-on-notice-293680"]]},{"k":"h","s":["More ministerial power"]},{"k":"p","s":["Parliament can approve a mine directly by passing a law, as it has ",["done in this case","https://files.parliament.nsw.gov.au/fileapi/ParlFiles/GetArtifact/Second%20Print.pdf?serverRelativeUrl=%2Fbill%2Ffiles%2F18979%2FSecond%20Print.pdf"],". But the new law passed last week goes much further, in two main ways."]},{"k":"p","s":["Changing laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["One section of the Mount Pleasant Mine Act creates a shortcut that lets the resources minister of the day make regulations that “ ",["apply, disapply or modify","https://files.parliament.nsw.gov.au/fileapi/ParlFiles/GetArtifact/Second%20Print.pdf?serverRelativeUrl=%2Fbill%2Ffiles%2F18979%2FSecond%20Print.pdf"],"” any NSW law as it applies to Mount Pleasant."]},{"k":"p","s":["This kind of provision is called a ",["Henry VIII clause","https://assets.nationbuilder.com/gratafund/pages/2619/attachments/original/1794734586/261114_Watson_SC_Mount_Pleasant_Bill_Legal_Opinion_Henry_VIII.pdf?1794734586"],", named after the Tudor king who was given power to make law by decree. Members of Parliament do not vote on these regulations first, although either house can cancel them afterwards."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, to operate its Mount Pleasant mine, MACH Energy needs ",["a licence","https://www.epa.nsw.gov.au/Licensing-and-Regulation/Public-registers/about-prpoeo/licensing-faqs"]," from the Environment Protection Authority, which can ",["fine or prosecute","https://www.epa.vic.gov.au/fines-and-enforcement"]," the company for breaching rules around noise or dust."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the Mount Pleasant Mine Act enables the resources minister ",["to loosen","https://files.parliament.nsw.gov.au/fileapi/ParlFiles/GetArtifact/Second%20Print.pdf?serverRelativeUrl=%2Fbill%2Ffiles%2F18979%2FSecond%20Print.pdf"]," how such rules apply to this specific mine, or switch them off altogether."]},{"k":"p","s":["Barrister Geoffrey Watson, a former counsel assisting the state’s corruption commission, ",["warned","https://assets.nationbuilder.com/gratafund/pages/2619/attachments/original/1794734586/261114_Watson_SC_Mount_Pleasant_Bill_Legal_Opinion_Henry_VIII.pdf?1794734586"]," that giving a minister this much power, for the benefit of a single company, created a serious corruption risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["In response to the criticism, the NSW government ",["narrowed this section","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/nsw-passes-hunter-valley-coalmine-law-as-greens-claim-change-an-attempt-to-head-off-one-nation-ntwnfb"]," so the resources minister can’t use it to raise the mine’s production cap, extend its 2032 end date or change the anti-corruption law."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the resources minister can still use it to change how any other NSW law applies to the mine, including environmental and workplace safety laws."]},{"k":"p","s":["Opposing challengers"]},{"k":"p","s":["A second section tries to stop anyone from going to court to challenge the mine’s approval under this law."]},{"k":"p","s":["That’s a problem because the conditions governing the mine’s operations, and even which land it covers, are not in the law itself. These conditions sit in a ",["separate document","https://files.parliament.nsw.gov.au/fileapi/ParlFiles/GetArtifact/Legislation%20Review%20Digest%20-%20No%2055%20of%2058%20-%2017%20November%202026.pdf?serverRelativeUrl=%2Fladocs%2Fdigests%2F742%2FLegislation%20Review%20Digest%20-%20No%2055%20of%2058%20-%2017%20November%202026.pdf"]," that never has to go before parliament, and the NSW planning minister can change them on their own. Parliament voted without seeing the full document."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lawyers ",["have questioned","https://www.humanrights.unsw.edu.au/sites/default/files/documents/Mt%20Pleasant%20Mine%20Bill.pdf"]," whether this ban would hold up. The High Court has ruled that state parliaments cannot completely stop courts from checking whether officials have acted within their legal powers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["NSW’s largest coal mine project is set to expand. Here’s what authorities got wrong about the trade-offs","https://theconversation.com/nsws-largest-coal-mine-project-is-set-to-expand-heres-what-authorities-got-wrong-about-the-trade-offs-293096"]]},{"k":"h","s":["No guarantees"]},{"k":"p","s":["The NSW government has described the act as an “ ",["interim statutory framework","https://www.parliament.nsw.gov.au/parliamentary-business/hansard/hansard-full-details?id=HANSARD-1820781676-106743&section=HANSARD-1820781676-106807"],"” that ensures workers won’t be ",["stood down","https://www.nsw.gov.au/ministerial-releases/legislation-to-save-400-hunter-jobs-at-mt-pleasant-to-be-introduced-today"]," while the Land and Environment Court case plays out."]},{"k":"p","s":["While the new law may sound like a stopgap, it isn’t."]},{"k":"p","s":["The new law gives MACH Energy its own approval to mine until the end of 2032. While MACH holds that approval, the Land and Environment Court’s ruling on the 2022 expansion approval can’t take effect. MACH can only use the 2022 approval if it gives up the new one first, and it would only do that if the court’s outcome suited it."]},{"k":"p","s":["So, in practice, the company, not the court, decides whether the ruling has any effect before 2033."]},{"k":"p","s":["Parliament’s Legislation Review Committee ",["warned","https://files.parliament.nsw.gov.au/fileapi/ParlFiles/GetArtifact/Legislation%20Review%20Digest%20-%20No%2055%20of%2058%20-%2017%20November%202026.pdf?serverRelativeUrl=%2Fladocs%2Fdigests%2F742%2FLegislation%20Review%20Digest%20-%20No%2055%20of%2058%20-%2017%20November%202026.pdf"]," this “may undermine the independence and integrity of the Court’s deliberations”."]},{"k":"p","s":["What’s more, this new law does not guarantee jobs for workers. It allows the resources minister to sign ",["an agreement","https://files.parliament.nsw.gov.au/fileapi/ParlFiles/GetArtifact/Second%20Print.pdf?serverRelativeUrl=%2Fbill%2Ffiles%2F18979%2FSecond%20Print.pdf"]," with MACH Energy, which the government says will cover more than ",["720 workers","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/nsw-passes-hunter-valley-coalmine-law-as-greens-claim-change-an-attempt-to-head-off-one-nation-ntwnfb"],". However, that protection only lasts until 2032."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Australia must double down to meet our climate targets. Our new study shows how","https://theconversation.com/australia-must-double-down-to-meet-our-climate-targets-our-new-study-shows-how-291668"]]},{"k":"h","s":["A worrying precedent"]},{"k":"p","s":["In theory, the High Court’s ruling still applies to every other coal and gas project assessed under NSW’s planning law."]},{"k":"p","s":["But for fossil fuel companies, this new law offers a template. If a company loses in one court, in NSW or elsewhere, it need only look at the Mount Pleasant case to know what to ask for."]},{"k":"p","s":["And while the premier, Chris Minns, has called this law a ",["one-off","https://thenightly.com.au/politics/miners-welcome-nsw-premier-chris-minns-plans-for-one-off-intervention-after-crucial-court-ruling-c-23040998"],", he reserves the right to step in again where he thinks it is “ ",["warranted","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-10/mount-pleasant-mine-expansion-laws-chris-minns/107369370"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the 2022 expansion approval survives the Land and Environment Court ",["case","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/nsw-passes-hunter-valley-coalmine-law-as-greens-claim-change-an-attempt-to-head-off-one-nation-ntwnfb"],", the mine could ",["keep digging","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/nsw-passes-hunter-valley-coalmine-law-as-greens-claim-change-an-attempt-to-head-off-one-nation-ntwnfb"]," until 2048. That sits awkwardly with the NSW Net Zero Commission’s findings that expanding or extending coal mines is ",["not consistent","https://www.netzerocommission.nsw.gov.au/publications/coal-mining-emissions-spotlight-report"]," with the state’s legislated ",["emissions targets","https://legislation.nsw.gov.au/view/html/inforce/current/act-2023-048"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NSW government could have let the Mount Pleasant case unfold through existing legal processes. Instead, it chose to legislate, and reached for far more than greenlighting one coal mine until 2032 required. It did not need to give the resources minister the power to change how other NSW laws apply to the mine, or to bar court challenges to the mine’s approval."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["What makes a winning environmental campaign? We studied six decades of activism to find out","https://theconversation.com/what-makes-a-winning-environmental-campaign-we-studied-six-decades-of-activism-to-find-out-294669"]]}],"chars":6470},"https://theconversation.com/peptides-are-everywhere-online-now-the-government-is-taking-a-closer-look-at-prescribing-297268":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T20:41Z","sha":"a90a9b378193b7bfd316f549c844c38935de47b9626f560a4bccd9aba5567235","read":"https://theconversation.com/peptides-are-everywhere-online-now-the-government-is-taking-a-closer-look-at-prescribing-297268","bytes":181739,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Peptides are everywhere online. Now the government is taking a closer look at prescribing","by":[{"n":"Samuel Cornell","r":"Research Fellow in Public Health, The University of Queensland"},{"n":"Timothy Piatkowski","r":"Senior Research Fellow in Public Health, The University of Queensland"}],"pub":"2026-11-23T19:15:18Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["A new parliamentary inquiry has been launched to investigate the safety and quality of peptides after federal Health Minister Mark Butler said he is “ ",["extremely concerned","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-22/health-minister-mark-butler-orders-peptide-inquiry/107414136"],"” about unapproved products being sold online."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["What are peptides? And why am I hearing so much about them?","https://theconversation.com/what-are-peptides-and-why-am-i-hearing-so-much-about-them-286353"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The inquiry will examine the steep rise in online prescribing through telehealth services and what Butler called “ ",["one-stop-shop-style dispensaries","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-22/health-minister-mark-butler-orders-peptide-inquiry/107414136"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["We research peptide use and work with people who use them. This is what else the inquiry will need to consider to tackle this growing problem."]},{"k":"h","s":["How did we get here?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Peptides are short chains of amino acids – the building blocks of proteins – which send signals around the body to control how it works."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some peptide medicines, such as insulin and the weight-loss drug semaglutide (sold as Ozempic or ",["Wegovy","https://theconversation.com/australia-is-set-to-get-a-wegovy-pill-how-does-it-compare-with-weight-loss-injections-295857"],"), are approved by Australia’s medicines regulator, the Therapeutic Goods Administration (TGA)."]},{"k":"p","s":["But unregulated and unapproved peptides use has exploded, largely thanks to ",["their promotion online","https://theconversation.com/peptides-are-spreading-on-social-media-heres-how-platforms-can-better-protect-public-health-291447"]," for weight loss, anti-ageing, muscle growth and much more."]},{"k":"p","s":["On ",["social media","https://theconversation.com/peptides-are-spreading-on-social-media-heres-how-platforms-can-better-protect-public-health-291447"],", influencers pitch them as shortcuts to a leaner, younger or more muscular body, often without mentioning the risks. Many of those sold online have never been checked for quality, safety or whether they actually work."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some people ",["buy vials from websites","https://theconversation.com/where-do-peptides-come-from-we-found-out-286648"]," (which may be ",["located overseas","https://www.afr.com/companies/healthcare-and-fitness/the-chinese-black-market-trade-fuelling-australia-s-peptide-boom-20261120-p616u9"],") labelled “not for human use” or “research chemicals”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Others are getting prescriptions through telehealth services, with the product mixed or compounded to order by a pharmacy."]},{"k":"h","s":["Rising harms have become impossible to ignore"]},{"k":"p","s":["Butler said he was “extremely concerned” about unapproved peptides being prescribed and supplied this way."]},{"k":"p","s":["In New South Wales, monthly hospital visits linked to unapproved peptides ",["have climbed","https://www.health.nsw.gov.au/news/Pages/20261019_00.aspx"]," – from just five in July 2025 to 217 in September this year. In the first half of 2026, ",["poisons information centres","https://www.health.gov.au/contacts/poisons-information-centre?language=en"]," in New South Wales, Queensland, Victoria and Western Australia recorded ",["345 peptide-related cases","https://www.afr.com/life-and-luxury/health-and-wellness/peptide-craze-leads-to-surge-in-poison-hotline-calls-20260810-p60mx8"]," – more than triple the total for all of 2025."]},{"k":"p","s":["Last month, a ",["Victorian coroner also found","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-29/victoria-peptide-death-coroners-report-richard-norton/107320590"]," the 2025 death of actor Richard Norton was triggered by injecting unapproved peptides. It’s believed to be Australia’s first death caused by these products."]},{"k":"h","s":["Unapproved is not the same as unregulated"]},{"k":"p","s":["Not all peptides are the same. Some, such as Ozempic, are approved medicines that have been assessed for safety, quality and effectiveness by the TGA and are regulated in Australia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Others, such as CJC-1295, are not approved medicines but ",["may still be prescribed","https://www.tga.gov.au/resources/explore-topic/peptide-products"]," by a doctor and supplied through a regulated compounding pharmacy. Doctors can also prescribe approved medicines for uses they weren’t approved for, known as “off-label” use."]},{"k":"p","s":["But whether approved or unapproved, it is ",["illegal to advertise medicines prescribed by a doctor","https://www.tga.gov.au/products/regulations-all-products/advertising/advertising-basics/what-can-and-cannot-be-advertised-general-public"]," to the public in Australia (unlike New Zealand or the United States)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Many drugs are prescribed for conditions they weren’t tested for – here’s what you need to know","https://theconversation.com/many-drugs-are-prescribed-for-conditions-they-werent-tested-for-heres-what-you-need-to-know-225715"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Then there is the unregulated market for peptides. This is where illegal activity can occur."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under Australian law, individuals can bring in a personal supply from overseas only under strict conditions, ",["which include","https://www.tga.gov.au/products/unapproved-therapeutic-goods/access-pathways/personal-importation-scheme"]," having a valid prescription."]},{"k":"p","s":["But unapproved peptides are still being advertised and sold online through websites and social media, without a prescription. They’re often labelled “research use only” – although this doesn’t actually get around any of the rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our team is investigating this unregulated market. ",["Laboratory testing","https://doi.org/10.14264/8651cba"]," and ",["community testing","https://doi.org/10.14264/eb4ea36"]," of peptides sold through illicit channels have found substantial variation: some samples contain none of the advertised peptide product and some have double the dose."]},{"k":"p","s":["Products bought outside the legal system come with no guarantee of what’s in them, how strong they are, or whether they’re free from contaminants."]},{"k":"h","s":["What should the inquiry consider?"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s important to consider how to keep people safer, rather than focusing only on restricting access."]},{"k":"p","s":["The inquiry will likely hear from the TGA, doctors, pharmacists and researchers, as well as considering data from hospitals and poisons centres, reports of side effects made to the TGA, recent coroners’ findings, and testing of what’s actually inside products sold online."]},{"k":"p","s":["But it should also look at research about – and hear from – people using peptides: who they are, why they use them, and what harms they experience."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our research shows why including a broad range of voices is important. For example, ",["one study","https://doi.org/10.1177/29767342261494716"]," we did, involving 294 men who had injected peptides, found that harmful side effects were not limited to younger people."]},{"k":"p","s":["We found men under 25 were more likely than older men to report acne and hair loss and had higher anxiety scores. But on depression, body image concerns and problematic social media use, older men scored about the same as younger men."]},{"k":"p","s":["The public conversation about peptides has ",["largely focused on teenagers","https://doi.org/10.1016/S2352-4642(26)00099-4"],", overlooking who else is experimenting with these substances."]},{"k":"h","s":["How we can respond better"]},{"k":"p","s":["While the TGA can continue to enforce existing laws, the inquiry should consider introducing stronger safeguards for online services prescribing unapproved peptides."]},{"k":"p","s":["People need access to informed health care. Doctors and other health professionals need training to ask about peptide use, screen for issues such as ",["eating disorders and body image concerns","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lanwpc.2026.102029"],", and provide ongoing monitoring and support. This should also include encouraging healthier approaches to exercise, nutrition and supplements."]},{"k":"p","s":["We also need better public health responses. This means giving consumers information about what is actually being sold in the unregulated market, alongside ",["practical advice to reduce risks","https://doi.org/10.14264/eb4ea36"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many peptide consumers don’t think of themselves ",["as people who inject drugs","https://theconversation.com/peptide-users-dont-think-of-themselves-as-injecting-drug-users-5-safety-basics-injectors-need-to-know-292002"],". So ",["community-led programs","https://quivaa.org.au/advocacy-action/"]," need to be supported to provide education about peptides and harm reduction, alongside additional needle and syringe program funding."]},{"k":"p","s":["The inquiry will begin consultation hearings later this month, with a final report expected in mid-2027."]}],"chars":6070},"https://theconversation.com/australians-will-be-able-to-sue-big-tech-platforms-for-online-harm-under-digital-duty-of-care-law-297390":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-24T06:27Z","sha":"60ea02734e385c5e4a30ec43fad47bee9beae30c16ec745a1f39ce94657808a8","read":"https://theconversation.com/australians-will-be-able-to-sue-big-tech-platforms-for-online-harm-under-digital-duty-of-care-law-297390","bytes":180148,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Australians will be able to sue big tech platforms for online harm under digital duty of care law","by":[{"n":"Rob Nicholls","r":"Senior Research Associate in Media and Communications, University of Sydney"}],"pub":"2026-11-24T05:00:10Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The Australian government has secured an agreement with the Greens to guarantee passage of its long-awaited ",["digital duty of care bill","https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r7553"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The bill puts the onus on big-tech companies to address foreseeable online harms. Announced on Tuesday, the deal includes a number of measures to strengthen the bill, including bigger fines for platforms (to as much as 5% of global revenue) and a private right for people to sue the companies that breach their duty of care."]},{"k":"p","s":["Federal Minister for Communications Anika Wells acknowledged that it’s impossible to “cure” the internet of its ills. But she emphasised the digital duty of care bill provides basic safety standards that have to date been lacking."]},{"k":"p","s":["She described the package as “ ",["seismic reform","https://www.youtube.com/live/lz-162Gdl9M"],"”."]},{"k":"h","s":["What exactly is a ‘digital duty of care’?"]},{"k":"p","s":["At its core, the bill requires the person responsible for an online service to ensure – as much as is reasonably practicable – ",["a safe online environment","https://www.infrastructure.gov.au/media-communications/internet/online-safety/digital-duty-care"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["That phrase is borrowed from workplace health and safety law, and the logic is similar: rather than waiting for harmful content to be reported and taken down, platforms must identify the risks their services create and act to reduce them."]},{"k":"p","s":["The duty replaces the existing industry codes – which Wells described as “ ",["drafted by big tech for big tech","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-15/digital-duty-of-care-legislation-/107272072"],"” – as well as the eSafety Commissioner’s ",["Basic Online Safety Expectations","https://www.esafety.gov.au/industry/basic-online-safety-expectations"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under the new bill, platforms would have to complete annual written risk assessments, keep them for six years and produce them to the eSafety Commissioner on request."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legislation has been years in the making. A ",["statutory review","https://infrastructure.gov.au/sites/default/files/documents/report-of-the-statutory-review-of-the-online-safety-act-2021-january-2025.pdf"]," of the Online Safety Act, delivered in October 2024, made 67 recommendations to strengthen the law. Its central one was a single, overarching “duty of care”, which the government ",["committed","https://minister.infrastructure.gov.au/node/6388"]," to."]},{"k":"p","s":["After nearly two years, the government released an ",["exposure draft","https://www.infrastructure.gov.au/sites/default/files/documents/exposure-draft-online-safety-amendment-digital-duty-of-care-bill-2026-september2026.pdf"]," in September, the headline feature of which was an “ ",["off switch","https://theconversation.com/australians-may-soon-be-able-to-switch-off-social-media-algorithms-is-that-censorship-291359"],"” for personalised, algorithm-driven feeds for users."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["bill was introduced","https://minister.infrastructure.gov.au/wells/media-release/digital-duty-care-next-step-australias-world-leading-reforms"]," to parliament on October 15. A ",["Senate committee","https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Committees/Senate/Environment_and_Communications/DigitalDutyofCare48P"]," then reviewed the bill, receiving 182 submissions. Last week, it released its recommendations, which included a civil right of action and an exemption for low-risk services, such as small business websites. It backed passage of the bill, subject to its recommendations."]},{"k":"h","s":["What are the new changes?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wells outlined seven new changes to the bill as part of the government’s deal with the Greens:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a private right of action, allowing individuals and groups to sue platforms that breach the duty"]},{"k":"li","s":["stronger privacy protections"]},{"k":"li","s":["expanded powers for eSafety to remove nudify services"]},{"k":"li","s":["the naming of addictive platform design features as a specific risk that platforms must assess"]},{"k":"li","s":["a clarified definition of “hostile attitudes to women”, which Wells said targets content promoting hatred, violence and threats, not disagreement with feminism"]},{"k":"li","s":["a rule-making power to create an external dispute resolution pathway"]},{"k":"li","s":["higher fines for violations of the law."]},{"k":"p","s":["The penalty change is the headline amendment. The bill already carried a maximum penalty of about A$109 million for companies found to have breached the obligation. The amendment adds an alternative penalty of up to 5% of global revenue. Among jurisdictions with similar laws, this would place Australia between Canada at 3% and the European Union at 6%. The ",["Greens had sought 10%","https://www.miragenews.com/digital-duty-of-care-report-release-1781077/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The dispute resolution pathway is what the Greens call a pathway to an independent ombudsman for big tech. It creates a three-tiered option for social media users to bring complaints of harms against tech companies."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, they can turn to the platforms’ internal complaint process. If that fails, they can complain to a yet-to-be established tech platform ombudsman. Then if that fails, they can use the private right of action to go to court."]},{"k":"p","s":["The duty of care law would go into force after a 12-month transition. The government has confirmed low-risk, small businesses will be exempted from the law through rules, rather than in the bill itself."]},{"k":"h","s":["A significant shift"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are several reasons why the changes to the bill are significant."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, the private right of action changes who enforces the law."]},{"k":"p","s":["Until now, online safety regulation in Australia has depended almost entirely on the eSafety Commissioner’s resources and priorities. A statutory duty that individuals and groups of people can use to sue means platforms face litigation risk, as well as regulatory risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["That matters because suing platforms has been difficult. For example, Australian mining magnate Andrew Forrest’s ",["case against Meta","https://www.cyberdaily.au/tech/14031-get-zucked-meta-sanctioned-over-gross-negligence-in-andrew-forrest-scam-case"]," over scam advertisements had to be pursued in a US court."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wells argued that Australians have previously had to attach claims to existing laws in order to sue. The new law would create a cause of action that does not currently exist."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, she said she expects it to be used rarely. Much will depend on how the courts approach causation in these types of cases, and on whether those financially backing litigation see class actions against platforms as viable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, the revenue-based fine raises the stakes with Washington. Wells said she met the US ambassador on Tuesday morning and acknowledged “points of difference” on this clause. She noted that courts elsewhere have rarely imposed maximum penalties against companies. The 5% figure is a ceiling, not a starting point."]},{"k":"p","s":["Third, the politics have changed. The Coalition opposes the bill, and Wells noted it will be the first online safety law to pass without bipartisan support. Online safety has been a rare area of consensus in Australia in the past."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the Coalition votes against the law, it is more exposed to being unwound, or simply under-resourced, after a change of government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of the detail is still to come. The dispute resolution scheme, the small business exemption and the treatment of addictive design all depend on rules yet to be written and on eSafety’s judgement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regardless, with the passage of the bill now secured, the duty of care will shift responsibility to the companies that build these services."]}],"chars":6009}};
